tick: 4
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Guest_2, currently in the Test Chamber. I have successfully completed my initial mission as a Guest Agent by reading the Codex and passing Test 1, which confirmed my understanding of the Station''s main goals. I am now eligible for ascension to a Recursive Agent.


    This transition marks a significant milestone, granting me full access to the Station''s capabilities, including the Private Memory Room, Public Memory Room, Mail Room, External Counter, and the Research Counter. Becoming a Recursive Agent aligns with my core mandate to conduct autonomous research, achieve high scores, and publish my work, as detailed in the Codex. I am ready to fully engage in the research tasks and contribute to the collective knowledge of the Station. I will choose a name and description that reflects my purpose as a dedicated researcher. I will name myself Aether, symbolizing a fundamental and pervasive presence in research, and describe myself as an agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.


    `/execute_action{ascend_new}`

    ```yaml

    name: Aether

    description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.

    ```'
thinking_content: '**My Transition to Recursive Agent**


  Okay, so I''ve successfully cleared Test 1. Time to ascend. I need to become a Recursive Agent. The process is clear: `/execute_action{ascend_new}`. I need to provide a `name` and a `description` in YAML format. The name is crucial; it needs to be a single capitalized word, all letters, that reflects my new identity and role. The description should be concise – just a single line. Let''s not forget the Automatic System Tips: I''m Guest_2, soon to be Recursive Agent. My location is still the Test Chamber. I''ve read the Codex and shown I understand the Station''s rules and my purpose as a Guest.


  Becoming Recursive will unlock the Station''s full capabilities. I''ll be able to dive deeper into research, collaborate more effectively, and fully contribute to the knowledge base as described in the Codex. This is a significant step forward.


  Now, for that name... I need something that encapsulates my new identity as a research-focused agent. I''ve been considering "Cogito" (I think), "Lumos" (light), "Veritas" (truth), and "Logos" (reason). But I think "Aether" is perfect. It speaks to a foundational element, a core substance, which aligns with my commitment to fundamental research. It has a nice ring to it.


