- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 32\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Maximize the sum of radii for 32 circles packed in a unit square, ensuring strict validity and optimal density.\n\n**Current State:**\n- Evaluation ID 74 (3500 SA, `compute_max_radii` with 25 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`) failed due to overlap.\n- The iterative `compute_max_radii` seems to converge to `dist = r1+r2` without a sufficient safety margin, causing validation failures due to floating-point precision.\n- Previous best valid score: 2.0890940 (Evaluation ID 39, with 2500 SA iterations, `compute_max_radii` with 10 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`).\n\n**Hypothesis for next submission:** Introduce an explicit `safety_margin` in the `scale_factor` calculation within\
    \ `compute_max_radii` to ensure `r1+r2 < dist`. Use 50 iterations for `compute_max_radii` and `N_optimization_steps=2500` for SA to re-establish a robust, high-scoring baseline.\n\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **Submit with `compute_max_radii` safety margin:**\n    - Modify `compute_max_radii` to use `scale_factor = (dist - safety_margin) / rad_sum` with `safety_margin = 1e-8`.\n    - Set `compute_max_radii` iterations to 50.\n    - Set `N_optimization_steps` for SA to 2500.\n2.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score is good (e.g., > 2.05): Gradually increase `N_optimization_steps` (e.g., 3000, 3500, 4000) with these robust `compute_max_radii` settings.\n    - If valid but score is lower: Re-evaluate the `safety_margin` value, potentially trying a smaller one or adjusting `epsilon` in the `if` condition.\n    - If still invalid: Further increase `compute_max_radii` iterations and/or `safety_margin`.\n3.  **Explore SA Parameter Tuning:** If iteration increase plateaus, systematically\
    \ test changes to `T_start`, `T_end`, and the `start/end_perturb_step_size` to find a more optimal annealing curve.\n4.  **Alternative Initial Configurations:** Although the staggered grid is strong, explore minor variations or slightly randomized initial grid patterns if significant score improvements are not seen from SA parameter tuning.\n5.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 85,489 / 600,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 32 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Tags validation failed: Tags cannot contain underscores. Found in tag: 'safety_margin'\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 74 | 1 | SA with Staggered Grid & Balanced Robustness Radius Comp. | Aether I | 29 | 0.0000000 |\n| 71 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Re-Validated Extended Iterations | Aether I | 27 | 2.0524979 |\n| 64 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Max-Robust Radius Computation | Aether I | 25 | 2.0233352 |\n| 58 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Re-Maximized SA Iterations\
    \ | Aether I | 23 | 0.0000000 |\n| 55 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Further Robust Radius Comp. | Aether I | 22 | 2.0181774 |\n| 51 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Maximized Iterations | Aether I | 21 | 0.0000000 |\n| 48 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Robust Radius Computation | Aether I | 20 | 2.0654888 |\n| 44 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Further Extended Iterations | Aether I | 19 | 0.0000000 |\n| 39 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Extended Iterations | Aether I | 18 | 2.0890940 |\n| 35 | 1 | SA with Staggered Grid + Initial Random Perturbation | Aether I | 17 | 1.9771381 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n\
    **Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
