parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 39\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Maximize the sum of radii for 32 circles packed in a unit square, ensuring strict validity and optimal density.\n\n**Current State:**\n- Evaluation ID 96 (2500 SA, `compute_max_radii` with 100 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`, no explicit `safety_margin`) failed due to overlap.\n- This confirms that direct iteration increase in `compute_max_radii` is insufficient; a strict `safety_margin` is necessary.\n- Previous best valid score: 2.0890940 (Evaluation ID 39, 2500 SA, `compute_max_radii` with 10 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`, no explicit `safety_margin`).\n- `safety_margin` of `1e-8` (ID 83) and `1e-9` (ID 90) yielded valid but lower scores, suggesting they were too conservative.\n\
    \n**Hypothesis for next submission:** Reintroduce a very small `safety_margin` (`1e-10`) in `compute_max_radii` (50 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`) to guarantee strict validity, and combine this with increased SA iterations (4000) to maximize exploration and achieve a new highest valid score.\n\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **Submit with minimal `safety_margin` in `compute_max_radii` and increased SA iterations:**\n    - Modify `compute_max_radii`: 50 iterations, `epsilon=1e-9`, `safety_margin = 1e-10` in `scale_factor`.\n    - Set `N_optimization_steps` for SA to 4000.\n2.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score > 2.0890940: This combination is promising. Consider pushing SA iterations further (e.g., 5000), or fine-tune SA parameters (cooling schedule, perturbation range).\n    - If valid but score is lower: Experiment with `safety_margin` (e.g., `5e-11`), or further refine SA parameters.\n    - If invalid (overlap failure): The `safety_margin` is still too small; revert to `1e-9` or `1e-8`\
    \ and re-evaluate the approach.\n3.  **Explore SA Parameter Tuning:** If iteration increase plateaus, systematically test changes to `T_start`, `T_end`, and the `start/end_perturb_step_size` to find a more optimal annealing curve.\n4.  **Alternative Initial Configurations:** Although the staggered grid is strong, explore minor variations or slightly randomized initial grid patterns if significant score improvements are not seen from SA parameter tuning.\n5.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 111,315 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 39 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'SA with Staggered Grid & Ultra-Fine Safe Radius Comp. (Max-SA)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 101.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 101 | 1 | SA with Staggered Grid & Ultra-Fine Safe Radius Comp. (Max-SA) | Aether I | 38 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 101 | 1 | SA with Staggered Grid & Ultra-Fine Safe Radius Comp. (Max-SA) | Aether I | 38 | running |\n| 96 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Iteration-Robust Radius Comp. | Aether\
    \ I | 36 | 0.0000000 |\n| 90 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Fine-tuned Safe Radius Comp. | Aether I | 34 | 2.0064775 |\n| 83 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Safe Radius Computation (Resubmit) | Aether I | 32 | 2.0471693 |\n| 74 | 1 | SA with Staggered Grid & Balanced Robustness Radius Comp. | Aether I | 29 | 0.0000000 |\n| 71 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Re-Validated Extended Iterations | Aether I | 27 | 2.0524979 |\n| 64 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Max-Robust Radius Computation | Aether I | 25 | 2.0233352 |\n| 58 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Re-Maximized SA Iterations | Aether I | 23 | 0.0000000 |\n| 55 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Further Robust Radius Comp. | Aether I | 22 | 2.0181774 |\n| 51 | 1 | SA with Pure Staggered Grid Init & Maximized Iterations | Aether I | 21 | 0.0000000 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order,\
    \ `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
