    \ increasing SA iterations to 5000 will allow for deeper exploration and achieve a new highest valid score, potentially surpassing 2.0890940.\n\n**TODO List:**\n1.  **Submit with increased SA iterations (5000):** Maintain robust `compute_max_radii` settings.\n2.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score > 2.0890940: This robust approach is optimal. Consider fine-tuning SA parameters (cooling schedule, perturbation range) or exploring minor initial configuration variations.\n    - If valid but score is lower/similar: Re-evaluate SA parameters. The current approach might be saturating the benefits of iteration increase, or the slight conservatism of the `safety_margin` is limiting.\n    - If invalid (overlap failure): Re-assess the `safety_margin` or `compute_max_radii` parameters if higher SA iterations introduce new edge cases.\n3.  **Explore SA Parameter Tuning:** If score plateaus, systematically test changes to `T_start`, `T_end`, and the `start/end_perturb_step_size` to find\
    \ a more optimal annealing curve.\n4.  **Alternative Initial Configurations:** Although the staggered grid is strong, explore minor variations or slightly randomized initial grid patterns if significant score improvements are not seen from SA parameter tuning.\n5.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 126,038 / 600,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 44 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'SA with Staggered Grid & Ultra-Fine Safe Radius Comp. (Max-SA, 6000 Iterations)' (ID: 112) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.103517223207091\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.103517\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System\
