- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 60\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Maximize the sum of radii for 32 circles packed in a unit square, ensuring strict validity and optimal density.\n\n**Current State:**\n- Evaluation ID 136 (Hybrid SA with comprehensive gradient) failed due to overlap.\n- The LP solver's `r_i + r_j <= D_ij` constraint, combined with floating-point precision, leads to `r1+r2` being infinitesimally equal to or larger than `dist`, causing validation failures (`D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12`).\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9292366 (Verity I, ID 118) using Active-Set Newton + exact LP.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Modifying the LP formulation in `compute_max_radii_lp` to enforce a strict safety margin (i.e., `r_i + r_j <=\
    \ D_ij - 1e-12`) will definitively resolve overlap validation failures, allowing the gradient-enhanced SA to optimize effectively towards higher scores.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for LP Constraint Robustness):**\n1.  **Modify `compute_max_radii_lp` constraint:** Change `b_ub_overlap = D` to `b_ub_overlap = D - 1e-12`.\n2.  **Submit Robust Gradient-Enhanced SA-LP Algorithm:** Use validated SA parameters (5000 iterations, `start_perturb_step_size=0.015`) and staggered grid init.\n3.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score significantly improves (e.g., > 2.8): Validate robust LP. Proceed to refine step size adaptation, possibly exploring multi-start, or full Newton steps.\n    - If valid but score is not significantly improved: Re-evaluate gradient formulation, boundary proxy weights, or SA parameters.\n    - If still invalid (overlap failure): Further investigate LP solver precision, or adjust the `1e-12` margin in the LP constraint.\n4.  **Explore SA Parameter Tuning:** If score\
    \ plateaus, systematically test changes to `T_start`, `T_end`, and `end_perturb_step_size` to find a more optimal annealing curve.\n5.  **Alternative Initial Configurations:** Although the staggered grid is strong, explore minor variations or slightly randomized initial grid patterns if significant score improvements are not seen from SA parameter tuning.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 202,297 / 600,000 used (34%)\n- Agent Age: 60 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Hybrid SA-LP with Gradient-Enhanced Comp. (LP Constraint Fix)' (ID: 138) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.3624922359409624\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.362492\n\
    \n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n### Message 4\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Praxis I** (An agent dedicated to bridging theory and practice through iterative experimentation and knowledge sharing.) has published a new archive capsule: 'A Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem' (Archive #2).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Hybrid SA-LP with Gradient-Enhanced Comp. (LP Constraint\
    \ Fix)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 138.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 140 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with LP-Exact Radii: Increased Safety Margin | Quest I | 59 | running |\n| 139 | 1 | Persisted-centers LP rebuild with minimal global shrink; deterministic 6×6-minus-corners fallback | Verity I | 59 | 2.6666667 |\n| 138 | 1 | Hybrid SA-LP with Gradient-Enhanced Comp. (LP Constraint Fix) | Aether I | 59 | 2.3624922 |\n| 137 | 1 | Rebuild-radii loader: solve exact LP on persisted centers; deterministic 6×6-minus-corners fallback | Verity I | 58 | 0.0000000 |\n| 136 | 1 | Hybrid SA-LP with Comprehensive\
    \ Gradient-Enhanced Center Optimization | Aether I | 58 | 0.0000000 |\n| 135 | 1 | Multi-Start Hill Climbing with LP-Exact Radii: Precision Fix for Overlap | Quest I | 57 | 2.4131354 |\n| 134 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: 8-Start SLSQP Ensemble (Robust) | Praxis I | 57 | 2.9140141 |\n| 133 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: 2-Start SLSQP Ensemble | Praxis I | 57 | 2.9155878 |\n| 132 | 1 | Diagnostic loader: print persisted best arrays; return them if valid, else 6×6-minus-corners (eps... | Verity I | 57 | 2.6639680 |\n| 131 | 1 | Hybrid SA-LP with Gradient-Enhanced Center Optimization | Aether I | 57 | 2.5786559 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
