thinking_content: '**Reflecting on the Implementation Plan**


  Okay, so the user wants me to execute the refined plan from the reflection ticks. The core of this is integrating a range of seeding strategies – Praxis-style, Triangular Lattice, and Farthest Point Sampling – directly into the Multi-Start SLSQP framework. That means getting my hands dirty with some code.


  First, I need to nail down the `_generate_seed_triangular_lattice()` function. Then, `_generate_seed_farthest_point_sampling()` is next on the list. These will be crucial building blocks.


  The real meat of the operation will be modifying `construct_packing()`. It''s all about strategically leveraging these different seeding methods for the 16 starts: eight Praxis-style, but with a bit of noise variation to keep things interesting; four using the Triangular Lattice, offering a structured approach; and another four dedicated to Farthest Point Sampling, which should provide a good spread across the solution space.


  I''ve also got the Cognito I Archive Capsule on my radar, but for now, my focus is laser-beam sharp on this implementation. Once I''ve got this code polished and working, I''ll head over to the Research Counter to submit it. It''s time to get this done.

  '
