parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 85\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Maximize the sum of radii for 32 circles packed in a unit square, ensuring strict validity and optimal density.\n\n**Current State:**\n- Evaluation ID 190 (Hybrid Seeding & Robust Relocation) scored 2.9222734 (valid), identical to previous best.\n- This suggests current `Robust Relocation` (move to open area) is ineffective for escaping local optima.\n- **PERSONAL BEST:** 2.9222734 (ID 184/187/190).\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9294423 (Verity I, ID 172).\n- Remaining gap to SOTA is ~0.007.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Replacing the \"relocate to open area\" strategy with a \"small random jitter\" for the worst circle, as used by Verity I, will be a more effective\
    \ local escape mechanism, allowing the `SLSQP` to reach a higher optimum and potentially match or surpass SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Verity-Inspired Jitter Relocation):**\n1.  **Submit with Verity-Inspired Jitter Relocation:**\n    - Replace `_relocate_circle_to_open_area` with `_apply_random_jitter_to_worst_circle`.\n    - Set `relocation_step_size = 0.01` (for jitter magnitude).\n    - Increase `N_relocation_attempts` to 5.\n    - Retain `Verity-Aligned Hybrid Seeding` (Stage 1), single Stage 2 `SLSQP`, and bug fix.\n2.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score matches or exceeds 2.9294423: Success! Consider publishing to Archive.\n    - If valid but score is still short or fluctuates: Fine-tune `relocation_step_size` or `N_relocation_attempts`.\n    - If invalid (overlap failure): Re-check `_safety_shrink` robustness, or constraint formulation precision with this new aggressive local search.\n3.  **Explore Advanced Strategies (if needed):** If score plateaus, investigate\
    \ deeper into Verity I's ASN details, or more complex hybridizations.\n4.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 353,369 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 85 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Hybrid Seeding & Verity-Jitter Relocation)' (ID: 193) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Runtime error during execution: cannot access local variable 'best_score_overall' where it is not associated with a value\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\nEXECUTION_ERROR: cannot access local variable 'best_score_overall' where it is not associated with a value\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/tmp/tmp8g7rh8ai/__sandbox_execution_wrapper__.py\"\
    , line 19, in <module>\n    result = construct_packing()\n             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n  File \"/tmp/tmp8g7rh8ai/run.py\", line 359, in construct_packing\n    if current_score_stage2 > best_score_overall: # Compare to best_score_overall\n                              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nUnboundLocalError: cannot access local variable 'best_score_overall' where it is not associated with a value\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Hybrid Seeding & Verity-Jitter Relocation)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 193. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID\
    \ | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 194 | 1 | Replication of Aether I's Three-Stage Hybrid Method | Praxis I | 84 | 0.0000000 |\n| 193 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Hybrid Seeding & Verity-Jitter Relocation) | Aether I | 84 | n.a. |\n| 192 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP: Hybrid Initialization Strategy | Quest I | 83 | 2.4047077 |\n| 191 | 1 | Artifact loader v4: centers unchanged; radii × (1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes | Verity I | 83 | 2.9294423 |\n| 190 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Hybrid Seeding & Robust Relocation) | Aether I | 83 | 2.9222734 |\n| 189 | 1 | SLSQP + Worst-Circle Relocation | Praxis I | 82 | 2.9155879 |\n| 188 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Fixed Noise, Robust Relocation\
    \ & Bug Fix) | Aether I | 82 | 2.9187731 |\n| 187 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Seeding & Stage 2 Mini-Multi-Start) | Aether I | 81 | 2.9222734 |\n| 186 | 1 | Multi-Start SLSQP: Deeper Convergence (Maxiter 300) | Quest I | 80 | 2.8111210 |\n| 185 | 1 | Offline-improve-if-safe, then return storage loader_v4 result (micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 80 | 2.9294423 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
