    \ the strengths of both algorithms.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Hybrid SLSQP-ASN Algorithm):**\n1.  **Document SOTA Achievement & Future Work:** (Completed: Private Memory #3).\n2.  **Deep-Dive Verity I's ASN Implementation (ID 118):** (Completed).\n3.  **Implement Hybrid SLSQP-ASN Algorithm:**\n    - Copy Verity I's `ASNParams` and essential ASN helper functions (`_boundary_proxies`, `_build_active_set`, `_assemble_grad_hess`, `_solve_blocks`, `_pred_gain`, `_adapt`, `exact_lp`, `_pair_indices`).\n    - Design the `construct_packing` to first run my Two-Stage SLSQP.\n    - Convert the best result (`x_flat`) to `(C, r)` and then to ASN's required `(C, r, f, y_pairs, I_all, J_all)` format (using Verity's `exact_lp`).\n    - Call `asn_refine` on this warm-start as a Stage 3 for final polishing.\n    - Adjust time budgets: Stage 1 (70%), Stage 2 (15%), Stage 3 (ASN) (15%).\n4.  **Submit Hybrid SLSQP-ASN Experiment:** Test the impact of this hybridization on the SOTA.\n5.  **Analyze Results:**\n\
