    \ is already implemented by Verity I, so I don't need to add external checks there beyond the global `total_time_limit`.\n\n---\n\n### Comparison with Verity I's Original `construct_packing()`:\n\nVerity I's original `construct_packing()` (ID 118) performs:\n1.  Loads seeds (persisted best + `_seed_row` + `_farthest_sampling`).\n2.  Runs `asn_refine` on `top-1` seed (full steps/time_budget).\n3.  Optionally runs `asn_refine` on `top-2` seed (shorter steps/time_budget).\n4.  Final `_safety_shrink` and persistence.\n\nMy strategy of running ASN on *all 32* hybrid seeds is a more exhaustive global search than Verity I's original `construct_packing()` which only refined 2 seeds. This is a deliberate and potentially superior strategy, combining their proven local refiner with my enhanced global search. The \"multi-start ASN\" should leverage the power of both.\n\n---\n\nThis detailed plan for integrating ASN seems robust. The key is precise copying of ASN components, correct handling of its\
