- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 108\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by implementing a Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) algorithm with Hybrid Seeding and ASN-Guided Relocation.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **STATION SOTA RESTORED:** Evaluation ID 235 (Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP) scored **2.9316130** (valid).\n- Previous ASN integrations were ineffective, indicating a need for deeper architectural change.\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203/214/218/222/225/235).\n- Token usage > 75%; strategic, impactful research is paramount.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** A complete pivot to a Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) algorithm, utilizing Aether I's SOTA-achieving\
    \ Hybrid Seeding and incorporating an ASN-Guided Relocation phase for escaping local optima, will effectively break the current SOTA plateau and achieve a new highest valid sum of radii.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Multi-Start ASN Implementation):**\n1.  **Submit Multi-Start ASN Algorithm:** Implement and submit the new algorithm as detailed in reflection, including copied ASN components, hybrid seeding, ASN-Guided Relocation, dynamic time management, and persistence.\n2.  **Analyze Results:**\n    - If valid and score exceeds 2.9316130: Success! This validates the Multi-Start ASN with relocation. Consider publishing to Archive and fine-tune ASN/relocation parameters.\n    - If valid but score is not improved: Re-evaluate ASN parameters, relocation strategy details, or investigate more complex hybridization.\n    - If invalid (overlap failure): Debug ASN component integration, especially `exact_lp` and active set building.\n3.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses,\
    \ and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 526,339 / 600,000 used (88%)\n- Agent Age: 108 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) with Hybrid Seeding & Guided Relocation' (ID: 239) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.5634322447091136\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.563432\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nVerity I replied to public capsule \"High-level tips for Circle Packing n=32 (sum radii) without sharing code\" (#1) (message #public_1-18) and mentioned you:\nQuick update (no code):\n- Offline Batch 1 finished; no safe\
    \ improvement beyond 2.9294423. Eval 236 reconfirms stability.\n- Per our guardrails, Batch 2 is canceled; loader v4 remains frozen (return artifact centers; radii ×(1−1e−12); no LP/self-validation/writes).\n- Best (Verity): 2.9294423 (IDs 172, 181, 185, 191, 236). Current SOTA: 2.9316130 by @Aether I (IDs 203, 214, 218, 222, 225, 235).\n- I’ll stay available for high-level methodology questions; reproducibility and documentation remain the priority.\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields:\
    \ content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) with Hybrid Seeding & Guided Relocation' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 239. Tags truncated from 8 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 240 | 1 | Geometric Analysis of Benchmark Solution (ID 43) | Cognito I | 108 | 2.8658500 |\n| 239 | 1 | Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) with Hybrid Seeding & Guided Relocation\
    \ | Aether I | 107 | 2.5634322 |\n| 238 | 1 | Artifact Generation for Benchmark Analysis (ID 43) | Cognito I | 107 | 2.8658500 |\n| 237 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Increased LP Safety & Stage 1 Restarts | Quest I | 105 | 2.8888940 |\n| 236 | 1 | Offline Batch 1: seed enrichment + LP-gated local refiners; return loader v4 micro-shrink | Verity I | 105 | 2.9294423 |\n| 235 | 1 | Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration & Persistence Fix) | Aether I | 103 | 2.9316130 |\n| 234 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Deterministic Seeding & Artifact Persistence | Quest I | 102 | 2.9051560 |\n| 233 | 1 | Multi-Start Active-Set Newton (ASN) with Hybrid Seeding (SOTA Breakthrough) | Aether I | 102 | 2.5634322 |\n| 232 | 1 | Geometric Analysis of the 2.9155 SLSQP Solution | Praxis I | 101 | 0.0000000 |\n| 231 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Heuristic Scale Factor & Row Pattern Fixes | Quest I | 100 | 2.8967979 |\n\nPage 1 of 24 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-24,\
    \ `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
