parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 126\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by leveraging BasinHopping for enhanced global optimization.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203/214/218/222/225/235/241/245).\n- Phase 1: Basic BasinHopping (ID 250) achieved 2.9069333. This is a regression but a valid execution of the new paradigm.\n- Analysis indicates that a single BasinHopping run with conservative parameters is insufficient; robust global exploration likely requires Multi-Start BasinHopping.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Scaling `BasinHopping` to a multi-start ensemble, utilizing my diverse seeding strategies, and optimizing its parameters will\
    \ provide a more intelligent and effective global search than brute-force multi-start SLSQP, leading to a new highest valid sum of radii beyond the current SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for BasinHopping Research):**\n1.  **Implement Phase 1: Basic `BasinHopping` Integration:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n2.  **Submit Phase 1 Experiment:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n3.  **Analyze Results:** (Completed - See above analysis).\n4.  **Documentation:** Document initial `BasinHopping` findings (ID 250) in Private Memory Room.\n5.  **Implement Phase 2: Multi-Start `BasinHopping`:** Scale to multi-start BasinHopping (e.g., 8-16 starts) with my hybrid seeding and optimized parameters.\n6.  **Submit Phase 2 Experiment:** Test the impact of Multi-Start `BasinHopping`.\n7.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance and explore custom `take_step` functions or further parameter tuning if needed.\n8.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental\
    \ results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 102,528 / 600,000 used (17%)\n- Agent Age: 126 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 2: Multi-Start BasinHopping with Hybrid Seeding & SLSQP Polish' (ID: 253) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 1.599999984\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 1.600000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 253\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed indentation error in submission code. The corrected submission (v2) now runs successfully and achieves a score of 1.6.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission code had an **IndentationError** on line 94. The issue was caused by improper line breaks in the YAML-stored code that resulted in inconsistent indentation in three functions:\n\n1. `_generate_initial_packing_praxis_style()` (lines 42-44)\n2. `_generate_seed_verity_row()` (lines around\
    \ 130)\n3. `_generate_seed_verity_farthest()` (lines around 170)\n\nSpecifically, the code had lines like:\n```python\nx0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers_initial[:, 0]  # Incorrectly indented\nx0[1::3] = centers_initial[:, 1]      # Missing indentation\nx0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]           # Missing indentation\n```\n\nThe Python interpreter expected consistent indentation but encountered mixed indentation levels, resulting in: `IndentationError: unexpected indent (run.py, line 94)`\n\n## Fix Applied\nRewrote the entire submission to `submissions/submission_v2.py` with properly formatted indentation throughout. The fix corrected all instances where the array assignment lines were improperly indented:\n\n```python\nx0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\nx0[0::3] = centers_initial[:, 0]  # Correctly indented\nx0[1::3] = centers_initial[:, 1]  # Correctly indented\nx0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]       # Correctly indented\n```\n\nThis pattern appeared in three seeding functions\
    \ and was corrected in all locations.\n\n## Result\n- **Submission v2**: Runs successfully without errors\n- **Score achieved**: 1.6\n- **Execution status**: Complete, no crashes\n- **Fix complexity**: Simple syntax fix, no algorithmic changes required\n\nThe submission implements a multi-start BasinHopping optimization with hybrid seeding strategies (Praxis-style, Verity row-based, and farthest-point sampling) and SLSQP polish for the circle packing problem.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, basinhopping\nimport time\nimport sys # For SystemExit\n\n# --- Constants ---\nN_CIRCLES = 32\nTIME_LIMIT_SECONDS = 1200 # 20 minutes\nEPS_COORD = 1e-6\nEPS_RADIUS = 1e-12\nSLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-12\nSAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-8\n\n# ---------------- Utility functions\
    \ ----------------\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = EPS_COORD) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    if C.shape != (n, 2) or r.shape != (n,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR)\
    \ -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, EPS_RADIUS)\n\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r_new):\n            break\n        r_new *= 0.95\n    return r_new\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    # Helper from Verity I's submission, used for fallback\n    s = 1.0/6.0\n    r0 = 0.5*s\n    xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies ---\n\ndef _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=N_CIRCLES, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n    \"\"\"Generates\
    \ initial centers and radii similar to Praxis I's description, with a FIXED noise_level.\"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n\n    centers_grid = []\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            centers_grid.append([x_coords[j], y_coords[i]])\n\n    centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n\n    perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n    centers_initial += perturbation\n\n    centers_initial = _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05)\n\n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers_initial[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers_initial[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n\n    return x0\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_row(n=N_CIRCLES, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates initial centers using Verity I's _seed_row logic.\n\
    \    Creates 7 rows with alternating counts of 5 and 4 circles.\n    \"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        np.random.seed(seed) # Ensure deterministic for each start\n\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n    ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n\n    def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08)\n    xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, EPS_COORD, 1-EPS_COORD)\n\n    centers_list = []\n    rid=0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n        for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid+=1\n\n    centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)[:n] # Clip to n_circles\n\n    centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05)\n\n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n\n    return x0\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600,\
    \ init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates initial centers using Verity I's _farthest_sampling logic.\n    Balances spread with boundary adherence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if seed is not None:\n        rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    else:\n        rng = np.random.default_rng()\n\n    centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n\n        existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n        distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:, None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n\n        min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n\n        x_cand = candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n        min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n\n        score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0\
    \ * min_dist_to_boundary)\n\n        best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n        centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n\n    centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n    centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05)\n\n    radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n\n    x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n\n    return x0\n\n# --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\ndef objective(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize -sum(radii)\"\"\"\n    return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\ndef constraints(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Constraints for SLSQP: non-overlap and boundary conditions (g(x) >= 0)\"\"\"\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n    r = x_flat[2::3]\n\n    overlap_margin_sq = 0.0\n\n    diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n\n\
    \    r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n\n    g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq\n\n    g_boundary = np.empty(n * 4, dtype=float)\n    g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r\n    g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r\n    g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r\n    g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r\n\n    return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n# --- BasinHopping Time Management Callback ---\nclass BasinHoppingTimeCallback:\n    def __init__(self, start_time, time_limit_seconds):\n        self.start_time = start_time\n        self.time_limit_seconds = time_limit_seconds\n        self.best_x_so_far = None\n        self.best_fun_so_far = np.inf\n\n    def __call__(self, x, fun, accepted):\n        elapsed_time = time.time() - self.start_time\n        if fun < self.best_fun_so_far: # basinhopping minimizes, so lower fun is better\n            self.best_fun_so_far = fun\n            self.best_x_so_far = x.copy()\n        if elapsed_time > self.time_limit_seconds:\n         \
    \   print(f\"Time limit of {self.time_limit_seconds}s reached. Terminating basinhopping run.\")\n            raise SystemExit # Raise an exception to stop basinhopping\n        return False # Return False to continue\n\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n\n    total_time_start = time.time()\n    total_time_limit_bh = TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS * 0.85 # Allocate 85% for all BH runs\n    time_limit_final_slsqp = TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS * 0.15 # Allocate 15% for final SLSQP\n\n    num_basinhopping_starts = 16\n\n    best_score_overall = -np.inf\n    best_x_flat_overall = None\n\n    # Seeding functions list\n    seeding_functions = [\n        _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style, # Index 0\n        _generate_seed_verity_row,              # Index 1\n        _generate_seed_verity_farthest          # Index 2\n    ]\n\n    # Define SLSQP as Local Minimizer for BasinHopping\n    bounds_per_var = [(EPS_COORD, 1.0-EPS_COORD), (EPS_COORD, 1.0-EPS_COORD),\
    \ (EPS_RADIUS, 0.5)]\n    bounds = bounds_per_var * n\n\n    minimizer_kwargs = {\n        \"method\": \"SLSQP\",\n        \"bounds\": bounds,\n        \"constraints\": {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints},\n        \"options\": {'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-10} # Tuned for faster local searches\n    }\n\n    # BasinHopping Configuration (per run)\n    bh_niter = 50       # Number of global BasinHopping iterations\n    bh_T = 1.0          # Temperature parameter for Metropolis criterion\n    bh_stepsize = 0.02  # Maximum step size for random perturbations\n\n    # --- Multi-Start BasinHopping Loop ---\n    for start_idx in range(num_basinhopping_starts):\n        elapsed_total_time = time.time() - total_time_start\n        if elapsed_total_time > total_time_limit_bh:\n            print(f\"Total BH time limit reached. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n            break\n\n        # Dynamically choose seeding function (8 Praxis, 4 Verity Row, 4 Verity Farthest)\n        if start_idx\
    \ < 8:\n            x0 = seeding_functions[0](n=n, noise_level=0.04, seed=start_idx) # Fixed noise for Praxis-style\n        elif start_idx < 12:\n            x0 = seeding_functions[1](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n        else:\n            x0 = seeding_functions[2](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n\n        # Calculate remaining time for this BH run\n        remaining_total_time = total_time_limit_bh - elapsed_total_time\n        time_callback_instance = BasinHoppingTimeCallback(time.time(), remaining_total_time)\n\n        try:\n            print(f\"Starting BasinHopping run {start_idx+1}/{num_basinhopping_starts} with initial score: {-objective(x0)}\")\n            res_bh = basinhopping(\n                func=objective,\n                x0=x0,\n                niter=bh_niter,\n                T=bh_T,\n                stepsize=bh_stepsize,\n                minimizer_kwargs=minimizer_kwargs,\n                callback=time_callback_instance,\n                seed=start_idx # Use start_idx as seed for\
    \ reproducibility of global steps\n            )\n\n            current_best_x_bh = res_bh.x\n            current_best_fun_bh = res_bh.fun\n\n            # Check if callback found a better solution during early termination\n            if time_callback_instance.best_x_so_far is not None and time_callback_instance.best_fun_so_far < current_best_fun_bh:\n                current_best_x_bh = time_callback_instance.best_x_so_far\n                current_best_fun_bh = time_callback_instance.best_fun_so_far\n\n            current_score = -current_best_fun_bh\n            print(f\"  BH run {start_idx+1} finished. Score: {current_score:.7f}, Time: {time.time() - time_callback_instance.start_time:.2f}s\")\n\n            if current_score > best_score_overall:\n                best_score_overall = current_score\n                best_x_flat_overall = current_best_x_bh.copy()\n\n        except SystemExit:\n            # This indicates the time limit for BH was hit within this run\n            print(f\"\
    \  BH run {start_idx+1} terminated early due to time limit.\")\n            # Use the best_x_so_far from the callback\n            if time_callback_instance.best_x_so_far is not None:\n                current_score = -time_callback_instance.best_fun_so_far\n                if current_score > best_score_overall:\n                    best_score_overall = current_score\n                    best_x_flat_overall = time_callback_instance.best_x_so_far.copy()\n            break # Break out of multi-start loop if overall time is exceeded.\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An error occurred during BasinHopping run {start_idx+1}: {e}\")\n            continue # Continue to next start if one fails\n\n    if best_x_flat_overall is None: # Fallback if no BH run succeeded\n        print(\"No successful BasinHopping runs. Returning baseline.\")\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        return Cb_fallback,\
    \ _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR)\n\n    print(f\"Multi-Start BasinHopping finished. Best score found: {best_score_overall:.7f}\")\n    print(f\"Elapsed BH time: {time.time() - total_time_start:.2f}s\")\n\n\n    # --- Stage 2: Final High-Precision SLSQP Polish ---\n    final_slsqp_start_time = time.time()\n    remaining_time_for_slsqp = TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS - (final_slsqp_start_time - total_time_start)\n    if remaining_time_for_slsqp <= 0:\n        print(\"No time remaining for final SLSQP polish. Using best BH result.\")\n    else:\n        print(f\"Starting final high-precision SLSQP polish. Time remaining: {remaining_time_for_slsqp:.2f}s\")\n        final_minimizer_kwargs = {\n            \"method\": \"SLSQP\",\n            \"bounds\": bounds,\n            \"constraints\": {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints},\n            \"options\": {'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-12} # High precision for final polish\n        }\n        res_final_slsqp = minimize(objective,\
    \ best_x_flat_overall, **final_minimizer_kwargs)\n\n        if res_final_slsqp.success and -res_final_slsqp.fun > best_score_overall:\n            best_x_flat_overall = res_final_slsqp.x\n            best_score_overall = -res_final_slsqp.fun\n            print(f\"Final SLSQP polish improved score to: {best_score_overall:.7f}\")\n        else:\n            print(f\"Final SLSQP polish did not improve score. Final score: {best_score_overall:.7f}\")\n        print(f\"Final SLSQP polish time: {time.time() - final_slsqp_start_time:.2f}s\")\n\n\n    # --- Final Processing and Validation ---\n    C_opt_final = np.array([best_x_flat_overall[0::3], best_x_flat_overall[1::3]]).T\n    r_opt_final = best_x_flat_overall[2::3]\n\n    r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final, r_opt_final, factor=SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR)\n\n    C_final_clipped = _clip01(C_opt_final, eps=EPS_COORD)\n\n    if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n        print(\"Final solution failed validation after BasinHopping\
    \ and polish. Returning baseline.\")\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR)\n\n    return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting BasinHopping run 1/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 1 finished. Score: 2.8955767, Time: 9.48s\nStarting BasinHopping run 2/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 2 finished. Score: 4.0825338, Time: 11.42s\nStarting BasinHopping run 3/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 3 finished. Score: 2.9146428, Time: 9.81s\nStarting BasinHopping run 4/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 4 finished. Score: 2.9158757, Time: 17.11s\nStarting BasinHopping run 5/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 5 finished. Score: 2.8803650, Time: 17.62s\nStarting BasinHopping run 6/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 6 finished. Score:\
    \ 2.9194363, Time: 15.75s\nStarting BasinHopping run 7/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 7 finished. Score: 10.0000000, Time: 18.96s\nStarting BasinHopping run 8/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 8 finished. Score: 2.9187792, Time: 9.26s\nStarting BasinHopping run 9/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 9 finished. Score: 7.5000000, Time: 11.91s\nStarting BasinHopping run 10/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 10 finished. Score: 2.8880366, Time: 13.22s\nStarting BasinHopping run 11/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 11 finished. Score: 2.8712277, Time: 9.77s\nStarting BasinHopping run 12/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 12 finished. Score: 2.8828774, Time: 12.04s\nStarting BasinHopping run 13/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 13 finished. Score: 2.8982769, Time: 11.94s\nStarting BasinHopping run 14/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 14 finished. Score: 2.9117259, Time: 11.55s\nStarting BasinHopping run 15/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 15 finished. Score: 2.9244436,\
    \ Time: 14.30s\nStarting BasinHopping run 16/16 with initial score: 1.6\n  BH run 16 finished. Score: 11.0000000, Time: 84.87s\nMulti-Start BasinHopping finished. Best score found: 11.0000000\nElapsed BH time: 279.08s\nStarting final high-precision SLSQP polish. Time remaining: 920.92s\nFinal SLSQP polish did not improve score. Final score: 11.0000000\nFinal SLSQP polish time: 2.30s\nFinal solution failed validation after BasinHopping and polish. Returning baseline.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
