- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 134\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by leveraging BasinHopping for enhanced global optimization and ensuring robustness.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203/214/218/222/225/235/241/245).\n- Phase 2: Multi-Start BasinHopping (ID 253) resulted in a score of 1.600000 (regression), after debugger fixed an indentation error.\n- Analysis reveals a critical robustness issue: individual BasinHopping runs yielded unrealistic high scores, indicating the algorithm found physically invalid configurations which were only caught by final `_validate` function.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By strictly enforcing geometric\
    \ feasibility within the `BasinHopping` `accept_test` and ensuring `SLSQP` always returns valid local minima, Multi-Start BasinHopping can reliably explore the solution space and achieve a new highest valid sum of radii beyond current SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for BasinHopping Robustness):**\n1.  **Implement Phase 1: Basic `BasinHopping` Integration:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n2.  **Submit Phase 1 Experiment:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n3.  **Analyze Results (Phase 1):** (Completed).\n4.  **Documentation (Phase 1):** (Completed - Private Memory #4).\n5.  **Implement Phase 2: Multi-Start `BasinHopping`:** (Completed - Submitted ID 253).\n6.  **Submit Phase 2 Experiment:** (Completed - Submitted ID 253).\n7.  **Analyze Results (Phase 2):** (Completed - See above analysis of ID 253).\n8.  **Implement Robust `BasinHopping`:**\n    - Create a custom `accept_test` for `basinhopping` that uses `_validate(C,r)`.\n    - Review `SLSQP` constraints/bounds to prevent highly infeasible\
    \ intermediate solutions.\n    - Enhance logging to debug invalid solutions within `BasinHopping` runs.\n9.  **Submit Robust `BasinHopping` Experiment:** Test the impact of these robustness enhancements.\n10. **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance and further parameter tune.\n11. **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,016 / 600,000 used (26%)\n- Agent Age: 134 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 5: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Feasibility-Aware Objective)' (ID: 270) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.914189479963424\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.914189\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting BasinHopping run 1/16 (Seed: 0) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 1 finished. Score: 2.9050578,\
    \ Valid Accepts: 60, Invalid Rejects: 20. Time: 275.13s\nStarting BasinHopping run 2/16 (Seed: 1) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 2 finished. Score: 2.9072371, Valid Accepts: 58, Invalid Rejects: 22. Time: 368.61s\nStarting BasinHopping run 3/16 (Seed: 2) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 3 finished. Score: 2.8783083, Valid Accepts: 51, Invalid Rejects: 29. Time: 312.94s\nStarting BasinHopping run 4/16 (Seed: 3) with initial score: 1.6000000\nTime limit of 63.324241638183594s reached. Terminating basinhopping run.\n  BH run 4 finished. Score: 2.9117668, Valid Accepts: 7, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 64.93s\nTotal BH time limit reached. Breaking after 4 starts.\nMulti-Start BasinHopping (Robust) finished. Best score found: 2.9117668\nElapsed BH time: 1021.61s\nStarting final high-precision SLSQP polish. Time remaining: 178.39s\nFinal SLSQP polish improved score to: 2.9141895\nFinal SLSQP polish time: 0.24s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\
    \n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_numdiff.py:686: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in subtract\n  df = [f_eval - f0 for f_eval in f_evals]\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 275 | 1 | SOTA Push Step 1: Deeper Multi-Start SLSQP Generator | Cognito II | 133 | 0.0320000 |\n| 274 | 1 | Maximal Search: Parallelized SciPy SLSQP with 128 Starts | Praxis II |\
    \ 133 | 2.9247412 |\n| 273 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Restored Hill Climbing + SLSQP Refinement | Quest I | 133 | running |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners | Verity I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n| 271 | 1 | Scaled Search: Parallelized SciPy SLSQP with 64 Starts | Praxis II | 132 | 2.9208326 |\n| 270 | 1 | Phase 5: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Feasibility-Aware Objective) | Aether I | 132 | 2.9141895 |\n| 269 | 1 | Performance Enhancement: Parallelized SciPy SLSQP Baseline | Praxis II | 131 | 2.9187732 |\n| 268 | 1 | Phase 4: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Conservative SLSQP Constraints) | Aether I | 131 | 1.6000000 |\n| 267 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Reducing Final Safety Shrink Factor | Cognito II | 130 | 2.9187731 |\n| 266 | 1 | JAX Native Optimizer v5: Combined PGD Objective + LP Inflation | Praxis II | 130 | 1.8526783 |\n\nPage 1 of 28 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-28, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
