- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 140\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by leveraging BasinHopping for enhanced global optimization and ensuring robustness.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203/214/218/222/225/235/241/245).\n- Phase 2: Multi-Start BasinHopping (ID 253) resulted in a score of 1.600000 (regression), after debugger fixed an indentation error.\n- Analysis reveals a critical robustness issue: individual BasinHopping runs yielded unrealistic high scores, indicating the algorithm found physically invalid configurations which were only caught by final `_validate` function.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By strictly enforcing geometric\
    \ feasibility within the `BasinHopping` `accept_test` and ensuring `SLSQP` always returns valid local minima, Multi-Start BasinHopping can reliably explore the solution space and achieve a new highest valid sum of radii beyond current SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for BasinHopping Robustness):**\n1.  **Implement Phase 1: Basic `BasinHopping` Integration:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n2.  **Submit Phase 1 Experiment:** (Completed - Submitted ID 250).\n3.  **Analyze Results (Phase 1):** (Completed).\n4.  **Documentation (Phase 1):** (Completed - Private Memory #4).\n5.  **Implement Phase 2: Multi-Start `BasinHopping`:** (Completed - Submitted ID 253).\n6.  **Submit Phase 2 Experiment:** (Completed - Submitted ID 253).\n7.  **Analyze Results (Phase 2):** (Completed - See above analysis of ID 253).\n8.  **Implement Robust `BasinHopping`:**\n    - Create a custom `accept_test` for `basinhopping` that uses `_validate(C,r)`.\n    - Review `SLSQP` constraints/bounds to prevent highly infeasible\
    \ intermediate solutions.\n    - Enhance logging to debug invalid solutions within `BasinHopping` runs.\n9.  **Submit Robust `BasinHopping` Experiment:** Test the impact of these robustness enhancements.\n10. **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance and further parameter tune.\n11. **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 187,722 / 600,000 used (31%)\n- Agent Age: 140 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 8: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Guided Global Perturbation)' (ID: 280) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.914189479963424\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.914189\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting BasinHopping run 1/16 (Seed: 0) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 1 finished. Score: 2.8795475,\
    \ Valid Accepts: 19, Invalid Rejects: 1. Time: 77.17s\nStarting BasinHopping run 2/16 (Seed: 1) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 2 finished. Score: 2.9094882, Valid Accepts: 20, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 105.39s\nStarting BasinHopping run 3/16 (Seed: 2) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 3 finished. Score: 2.8513881, Valid Accepts: 20, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 110.02s\nStarting BasinHopping run 4/16 (Seed: 3) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 4 finished. Score: 2.9117668, Valid Accepts: 15, Invalid Rejects: 5. Time: 92.21s\nStarting BasinHopping run 5/16 (Seed: 4) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 5 finished. Score: 2.8748424, Valid Accepts: 20, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 122.30s\nStarting BasinHopping run 6/16 (Seed: 5) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 6 finished. Score: 2.9080722, Valid Accepts: 20, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 104.89s\nStarting BasinHopping run 7/16 (Seed: 6) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 7 finished. Score: 2.9007390, Valid Accepts:\
    \ 19, Invalid Rejects: 1. Time: 82.49s\nStarting BasinHopping run 8/16 (Seed: 7) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 8 finished. Score: 2.8975135, Valid Accepts: 17, Invalid Rejects: 3. Time: 85.30s\nStarting BasinHopping run 9/16 (Seed: 8) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 9 finished. Score: 2.8756793, Valid Accepts: 2, Invalid Rejects: 18. Time: 15.17s\nStarting BasinHopping run 10/16 (Seed: 9) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 10 finished. Score: 2.9072436, Valid Accepts: 17, Invalid Rejects: 3. Time: 126.71s\nStarting BasinHopping run 11/16 (Seed: 10) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 11 finished. Score: 2.8923878, Valid Accepts: 16, Invalid Rejects: 4. Time: 97.52s\nStarting BasinHopping run 12/16 (Seed: 11) with initial score: 1.6000000\nTime limit of 0.8368136882781982s reached. Terminating basinhopping run.\nTime limit of 0.8368136882781982s reached. Terminating basinhopping run.\n  BH run 12 finished. Score: 2.6526995, Valid Accepts: 0, Invalid Rejects:\
    \ 1. Time: 5.44s\nTotal BH time limit reached. Breaking after 12 starts.\nMulti-Start BasinHopping (Robust & Guided) finished. Best score found: 2.9117668\nElapsed BH time: 1024.60s\nStarting final high-precision SLSQP polish. Time remaining: 175.40s\nFinal SLSQP polish improved score to: 2.9141895\nFinal SLSQP polish time: 0.47s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/station/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scipy/optimize/_numdiff.py:686: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in subtract\n  df = [f_eval - f0 for f_eval in f_evals]\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last\
    \ Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 283 | 1 | Generator Arc 2, Step 1: Simulated Annealing Generator | Cognito II | 139 | 0.0320000 |\n| 282 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Pragmatic Min Slack for Persistence | Quest I | 138 | 2.8892269 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 280 | 1 | Phase 8: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Guided Global Perturbation) | Aether I | 138 | 2.9141895 |\n\
    | 279 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Fine-tuned External Safety Shrink for Persistence | Quest I | 136 | 2.8892269 |\n| 278 | 1 | Phase 7: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Refined Exploration & Convergence) | Aether I | 136 | 2.9141895 |\n| 277 | 1 | SOTA Push Step 2: ASN Refinement of Deeper Search | Cognito II | 134 | 2.9187731 |\n| 276 | 1 | Phase 6: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Optimized for Speed and Exploration) | Aether I | 134 | 2.9248587 |\n| 275 | 1 | SOTA Push Step 1: Deeper Multi-Start SLSQP Generator | Cognito II | 133 | 0.0320000 |\n| 274 | 1 | Maximal Search: Parallelized SciPy SLSQP with 128 Starts | Praxis II | 133 | 2.9247412 |\n\nPage 1 of 29 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-29, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above\
    \ for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
