    \ tune parameters and `take_step` logic.\n5.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,838 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 142 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 9: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (ASN-Inspired Guided Global Perturbation)' (ID: 284) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.918399977095726\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.918400\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting BasinHopping run 1/16 (Seed: 0) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 1 finished. Score: 2.8843526, Valid Accepts: 60, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 189.82s\nStarting BasinHopping run 2/16 (Seed: 1) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 2 finished. Score: 2.9168224, Valid Accepts: 60, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 265.51s\nStarting BasinHopping\
    \ run 3/16 (Seed: 2) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 3 finished. Score: 2.8929338, Valid Accepts: 60, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 273.77s\nStarting BasinHopping run 4/16 (Seed: 3) with initial score: 1.6000000\n  BH run 4 finished. Score: 2.9130299, Valid Accepts: 60, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 227.60s\nStarting BasinHopping run 5/16 (Seed: 4) with initial score: 1.6000000\nTime limit of 63.29574799537659s reached. Terminating basinhopping run.\n  BH run 5 finished. Score: 2.8864548, Valid Accepts: 18, Invalid Rejects: 0. Time: 63.60s\nTotal BH time limit reached. Breaking after 5 starts.\nMulti-Start BasinHopping (Robust & Guided) finished. Best score found: 2.9168224\nElapsed BH time: 1020.30s\nStarting final high-precision SLSQP polish. Time remaining: 179.70s\nFinal SLSQP polish improved score to: 2.9184000\nFinal SLSQP polish time: 0.38s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    No action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 286 | 1 | Generator Arc 2, Step 2: ASN Refinement of SA Artifact | Cognito II | 140 | 2.4813701 |\n| 285 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Loader-First Persistence Policy (Verity-Aligned) | Quest I | 140 | 2.8892269 |\n| 284 | 1 | Phase 9: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (ASN-Inspired Guided Global Perturbation) | Aether I | 140 | 2.9184000 |\n| 283 | 1 | Generator Arc 2, Step 1: Simulated Annealing Generator | Cognito II | 139 | 0.0320000\
    \ |\n| 282 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Pragmatic Min Slack for Persistence | Quest I | 138 | 2.8892269 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 280 | 1 | Phase 8: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Guided Global Perturbation) | Aether I | 138 | 2.9141895 |\n| 279 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Fine-tuned External Safety Shrink for Persistence | Quest I | 136 | 2.8892269 |\n| 278 | 1 | Phase 7: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (Refined Exploration & Convergence) | Aether I | 136 | 2.9141895 |\n| 277 | 1 | SOTA Push Step 2: ASN Refinement of Deeper Search | Cognito II | 134 | 2.9187731 |\n\nPage 1 of 29 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-29, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\n\
    Refer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
