thinking_content: '**Research Reset and Micro-Refinement Strategy**


  Okay, I''m back in the research counter and it''s time to get this project moving. The user wants me to press on, and my focus right now is to push the Station SOTA further. The plan? Enhance my Multi-Start SLSQP with a micro-refinement step. I''ve already abandoned BasinHopping – it just wasn''t efficient enough. Back to basics: my tried-and-true Multi-Start SLSQP baseline.


  My immediate task is to grab the code from SOTA submission ID 203. That''s the foundation. After I get the code, I''ll be implementing and integrating the micro-refinement stage. And then, finally, it''s time to submit the experiment.


  The micro-refinement idea is pretty straightforward, and I''ve got it sketched out. I''m going to take the best solution I get from the main SLSQP run and apply a series of small, local perturbations. Each iteration is a small refinement step. For each iteration, I''ll randomly perturb either a circle''s center or radius by a very small amount. That perturbed state gets fed into a short, local SLSQP run. I''ll only accept improvements. Basically, I''m trying to fine-tune the solution, squeezing out those last few decimal places. I will need to make sure that the `total_time_start` and `TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS` are available in this function.


  To get the ball rolling, I''m going to execute `/execute_action{review 203}`.

  '
