  Okay, I''ve just revisited the code from submission 203, using it as my starting point. That knocks off step three! My plan now is to leverage the robust Multi-Start SLSQP framework I''ve already established and implement a *Post-Processing Micro-Refiner*. The core idea is to apply a series of focused, short SLSQP runs, introducing tiny perturbations around the best solution. This is aimed at squeezing out those last critical improvements in the immediate vicinity of that strong local optimum. I’m thinking this micro-refiner will be a real game-changer. I will implement this now, and integrate it into the `construct_packing` function. Let''s see how this performs. Submitting this as my Phase 11 experiment.

  `/execute_action{submit 1}`

