parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 150\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by enhancing my Multi-Start SLSQP with a post-processing micro-refinement stage.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 256/259). My previous SOTA was 2.9316130 (ID 203).\n- Phase 10: Robust Multi-Start BasinHopping (ID 287) scored 2.9184000.\n- Analysis indicates BasinHopping is too slow/inefficient for current constraints. Reverting to proven Multi-Start SLSQP baseline.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By building upon my SOTA Multi-Start SLSQP algorithm (ID 203) and integrating a post-processing \"micro-refiner\" (e.g., iterative, short, targeted SLSQP runs with small perturbations,\
    \ inspired by coordinate descent), I can achieve a slight but critical improvement beyond current SOTA by efficiently exploring the immediate vicinity of the strong local optimum.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Hybrid SLSQP + Micro-Refiner):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 10):** (Completed).\n2.  **Document BasinHopping Findings:** Document the challenges and limited success of `BasinHopping` in Private Memory, concluding it's not the most efficient path to SOTA for current constraints and prompting a return to SLSQP-centric research.\n3.  **Revert to SOTA Multi-Start SLSQP Baseline:** Use the code from my SOTA submission (ID 203) as the base for the `construct_packing` function.\n4.  **Implement Post-Processing Micro-Refiner (`_micro_refine_slsqp`):**\n    - It will take `x_flat_initial` from main SLSQP, `iterations` (e.g., 200), `step_factor` (e.g., 1e-4).\n    - Perform `iterations` of: pick a random circle, apply a small random perturbation to its center/radius, run a very short SLSQP,\
    \ accept only if better.\n    - Use `_slsqp_constraints` (with `overlap_margin_sq=-1e-12`).\n5.  **Integrate Micro-Refiner:** Apply `_micro_refine_slsqp` to the best solution from the main 32-start SLSQP (after Stage 1 and Stage 2) but *before* final `_safety_shrink` and `_validate`.\n6.  **Submit Phase 11 Experiment:** Test the impact of this Micro-Refiner.\n7.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance and fine-tune `_micro_refine_slsqp` parameters.\n8.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 236,615 / 600,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 150 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 11: Multi-Start SLSQP with Post-Processing Micro-Refiner' (ID: 296) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:**\
    \ 2.7850323410335607\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.785032\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 840.00s\nStage 1 finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 26.61s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish. Time budget: 180.00s\n  Stage 2 improved score to: 2.9316130\n  Stage 2 polish time: 1760826970.43s\nStarting Micro-Refiner. Initial score: 2.9316130. Time budget: 180.00s\nMicro-Refiner finished. Best score after refinement: 2.9316130. Time: 19.71s\nOptimization finished. Final score before validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 46.38s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n\
    **Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 11: Multi-Start SLSQP with Post-Processing Micro-Refiner' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 296.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 297 | 1 | Generator Arc 4, Step 2: ASN Refinement of Hybrid Seed | Cognito II | 149 | running |\n| 296 | 1 | Phase 11: Multi-Start SLSQP with Post-Processing Micro-Refiner | Aether I | 149 | 2.7850323 |\n| 295 | 1 | Generator Arc 4, Step 1 (Corrected): Hybrid Physics+SLSQP | Cognito II | 148 | 0.0320000 |\n| 294 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Basin-Hopping (Powell) Global + SLSQP Refinement | Quest I | 148 | 2.8892269 |\n| 293 | 1 | Generator\
    \ Arc 4, Step 1: Hybrid Physics+SLSQP Generator | Cognito II | 147 | 0.0320000 |\n| 292 | 1 | Final Pre-Maturity Test: Deeper Refinement of Parallel SLSQP | Praxis II | 145 | 2.9247412 |\n| 291 | 1 | Generator Arc 3, Step 2: ASN Refinement of Physics Seed | Cognito II | 144 | 2.4813701 |\n| 290 | 1 | Revisiting JAX PGD: Scaled Search and Increased Penalty | Praxis II | 144 | 2.1920953 |\n| 289 | 1 | Generator Arc 3, Step 1: Physics-Based Seed Champion | Cognito II | 143 | 0.0320000 |\n| 288 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Force Search for Higher SOTA (Loader-First) | Quest I | 142 | 2.8892269 |\n\nPage 1 of 30 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-30, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
