parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 159\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Station SOTA beyond my current record by ensuring robust validation of my Multi-Start SLSQP solutions through ultra-fine epsilon tuning.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301, submitted at Tick 153). My previous SOTA was 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203).\n- My Phase 13 submission (for enhanced validation debugging, also ID 301) was lost/overwritten by the system.\n- Latest successful experiment (Phase 12, ID 298) scored 2.7850324 (regression), confirming persistent validation failure for SOTA-level solutions.\n- Inferred root cause: Insufficiently strict `_validate` epsilon and/or safety shrink factor.\n\n**Hypothesis\
    \ for Next Breakthrough:** By setting `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16` (to match platform's implied strictness) and `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-14` (to provide a robust buffer), I can restore my SOTA. This will ensure high-quality solutions pass final validation, creating a stable baseline to then surpass Verity I's SOTA with a micro-refiner.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Validation Fix & SOTA Restoration):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 12, ID 298):** (Completed - confirmed validation failure).\n2.  **Document Phase 12 Findings:** Document in Private Memory.\n3.  **Implement Phase 13: SOTA Restoration - Enhanced Validation Debug:** (Completed - Submission lost).\n4.  **Submit Phase 13 Experiment:** (Completed - Submission lost).\n5.  **Analyze Results (Phase 13):** (No logs available, assumed lost).\n6.  **Implement Phase 14: SOTA Restoration - Ultra-Fine Validation Fix:**\n    - Set `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16`.\n    - Set `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-14`.\n    - Revert `construct_packing`\
    \ to ID 203 structure (without micro-refiner) to isolate validation fix.\n7.  **Submit Phase 14 Experiment:** Test the impact of this targeted validation fix.\n8.  **Analyze Results & Refine (Micro-Refiner Tuning):** If SOTA is restored, re-introduce and evaluate the performance of the micro-refiner and fine-tune its parameters.\n9.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 272,772 / 600,000 used (45%)\n- Agent Age: 159 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 14: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Ultra-Fine Validation Fix)' (ID: 307) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.785032363822878\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.785032\n\n\
    **Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 960.00s\nStage 1 finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 17.47s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish. Time budget: 240.00s. Elapsed: 17.47s\n  Stage 2 improved score to: 2.9316130\n  Stage 2 polish time: 0.14s\nOptimization finished. Final score before validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 17.60s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Phase 14: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Ultra-Fine Validation Fix)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing\
    \ in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 307. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 308 | 1 | Synthesis: Integrating Aether I's ASN Refiner with Parallel SLSQP | Praxis II | 158 | 2.9247411 |\n| 307 | 1 | Phase 14: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Ultra-Fine Validation Fix) | Aether I | 158 | 2.7850324 |\n| 306 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Re-establishing High Score (Post-Artifact Deletion) | Quest I | 157 | 2.8892269 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 304 | 1 | Hypothesis Test: Increasing Refiner Max Step Size (dmax)\
    \ | Cognito II | 155 | 2.9187731 |\n| 303 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Restoration of Proven Hill Climbing (Post-BasinHopping Reversal) | Quest I | 155 | 2.7099297 |\n| 302 | 1 | Analysis: Instrumenting the ASN Refiner Dynamics | Cognito II | 154 | 2.9187731 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 300 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Force Search (Basin-Hopping Stage 1) | Quest I | 150 | 2.7099297 |\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 31 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-31, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for\
    \ room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
