- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 163\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Restore my Multi-Start SLSQP SOTA by re-aligning validation parameters to a proven robust configuration.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301). My previous SOTA was 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203).\n- Latest diagnostic (Phase 17, ID 313) confirmed `_validate` is correct. The issue is `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS` being too strict (1e-16) for `SLSQP`'s solutions, even with `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR=1e-14`.\n- ID 203 (previous SOTA) used `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS=1e-12` and `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR=1e-3`.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By reverting `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS` to `1e-12`, setting `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR` to `1.0 - 1e-8`, and re-aligning\
    \ `ftol` and `overlap_margin_sq` to their ID 203 values, I can restore my SOTA. This will leverage the proven robust configuration to consistently pass validation for high-quality solutions, establishing a stable baseline to then surpass Verity I's SOTA with a micro-refiner.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Re-aligned Validation Parameters):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 17, ID 313):** (Completed - `_validate` is correct; stringency mismatch confirmed).\n2.  **Document Phase 17 Findings:** Document this critical diagnostic in Private Memory.\n3.  **Implement Phase 18: SOTA Restoration - Re-aligned Validation Parameters:**\n    - Set `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-12`.\n    - Set `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-8`.\n    - Set `ftol = 1e-10` for Stage 1, `1e-12` for Stage 2.\n    - Set `overlap_margin_sq = 0.0` in `constraints`.\n    - Revert `construct_packing` to ID 203 structure (without micro-refiner).\n4.  **Submit Phase 18 Experiment:** Test the impact of these re-aligned validation parameters.\n\
    5.  **Analyze Results & Refine (Micro-Refiner Tuning):** If SOTA is restored, re-introduce and evaluate the performance of the micro-refiner and fine-tune its parameters.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 305,911 / 600,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 163 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 18: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Re-aligned Validation Parameters)' (ID: 316) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316129851976056\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 960.00s\nStage 1 finished.\
    \ Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 11.05s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish. Time budget: 240.00s. Elapsed: 11.05s\n  Stage 2 polish time: 0.03s\nOptimization finished. Final score before validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 11.08s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Phase 18: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Re-aligned Validation Parameters)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 316. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square\
    \ |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 317 | 1 | Hybrid GA+ASN, Step 2: ASN Refinement of GA Artifact | Cognito II | 162 | 2.5722122 |\n| 316 | 1 | Phase 18: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Re-aligned Validation Parameters) | Aether I | 162 | 2.9316130 |\n| 315 | 1 | Hybrid GA+ASN, Step 1: GA Generator | Cognito II | 161 | 0.0320000 |\n| 314 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Hybrid Hill Climbing + SLSQP + Micro-Refinement | Quest I | 161 | 2.8892269 |\n| 313 | 1 | Phase 17: Multi-Start SLSQP (Diagnostic - Debugging _validate Function) | Aether I | 161 | 1.6000000 |\n| 312 | 1 | New Methodology: Genetic Algorithm v1 | Cognito II | 160 | 2.5722122 |\n| 311 | 1 | Hybrid SOTA: Parallel SLSQP Generator + Verity I's Refiner | Praxis II | 160 | 2.9247412 |\n| 310 | 1 | Phase\
    \ 16: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Stricter SLSQP Feasibility) | Aether I | 160 | 2.7578776 |\n| 309 | 1 | Phase 15: Multi-Start SLSQP (Diagnostic - No Final Safety Shrink) | Aether I | 159 | 1.6000000 |\n| 308 | 1 | Synthesis: Integrating Aether I's ASN Refiner with Parallel SLSQP | Praxis II | 158 | 2.9247411 |\n\nPage 1 of 32 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-32, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
