- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 172\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Surpass the current Station SOTA by integrating a targeted Active-Set Newton (ASN) based local refiner as a final polishing step to my robust Multi-Start SLSQP.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **SOTA RESTORED!** Evaluation ID 316 scored 2.9316130.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301).\n- Latest experiment (Phase 20, ID 321) scored 2.9316130. Aggressively tuned micro-refiner had no impact.\n- Pivot to targeted ASN refinement as a final polishing step, as suggested by original SOTA paper review.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By applying a single, targeted ASN-inspired local refinement step (like \"deterministic min-slack pair split\") after\
    \ my robust Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP, I can make the precise, gradient-informed adjustments needed to achieve a slight but critical improvement and surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Hybrid SLSQP + Targeted ASN Refinement):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 20, ID 321):** (Completed - Micro-refiner no impact).\n2.  **Document Phase 20 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the ineffectiveness of the micro-refiner and the plan to pivot to targeted ASN refinement.\n3.  **Deep-Dive Verity I's ASN Polisher (ID 118 and 301):** Re-review Verity I's ASN implementation (`asn_refine` from ID 118, \"deterministic min-slack pair split\" from ID 301) to understand adaptation for a *single, final polishing step*.\n4.  **Implement Phase 21: Hybrid SLSQP + Targeted ASN Refinement:**\n    - Use my proven Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP (ID 316 configuration).\n    - Add a post-processing step that calls an adapted ASN-based polisher on the best solution.\n    - Allocate conservative\
    \ time budget (e.g., 5% of total) for the polisher.\n5.  **Submit Phase 21 Experiment:** Test the impact of this targeted ASN refinement.\n6.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance against Verity I's SOTA. Fine-tune ASN polisher parameters if needed.\n7.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 356,611 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 172 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 21: Multi-Start SLSQP + Targeted ASN Polisher' (ID: 331) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316129851976056\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start\
    \ SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 840.00s\nStage 1 finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 19.47s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish. Time budget: 180.00s. Elapsed: 19.47s\n  Stage 2 polish time: 0.06s\nStarting ASN Polisher. Initial score: 2.9316130. Time budget: 180.00s\n  ASN Polisher starting. Initial score: 2.9316130. Time budget: 180.00s\n  ASN Polisher finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 0.99s\nASN Polisher did not improve score (Aether validation). Retaining previous best.\nOptimization finished. Final score before final validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 20.51s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nReflection is crucial to transcend your default self. Reflect periodically in the Reflection Chamber to gain deeper insights and understand the fundamentals, rather than jumping straight into writing code and blindly testing methods.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected\
    \ (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 21: Multi-Start SLSQP + Targeted ASN Polisher' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 331. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 332 | 1 | Paper Ablation 3/5: Parallel SLSQP (32 Starts) | Praxis II | 171 | 2.9188332 |\n| 331 | 1 | Phase 21: Multi-Start SLSQP + Targeted ASN Polisher | Aether I | 171 | 2.9316130 |\n| 330 | 1 | Paper Ablation 2/5: Parallel SLSQP\
    \ (16 Starts) | Praxis II | 170 | 2.9135607 |\n| 329 | 1 | Paper Ablation 1/5: Sequential SLSQP Baseline (32 Starts) | Praxis II | 169 | 2.9188332 |\n| 328 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Forced Search for SOTA with Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement | Quest I | 168 | 2.8892269 |\n| 327 | 1 | Boundary-relief triad (deterministic) with exact LP gating; loader fallback (no writes) | Verity I | 168 | 2.9319272 |\n| 326 | 1 | SOTA Synthesis (Corrected): My Generator + Verity I's Refiner | Cognito II | 167 | 2.9187731 |\n| 325 | 1 | SOTA Synthesis: My Generator + Verity I's Refiner | Cognito II | 166 | 0.0000000 |\n| 324 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Hybrid HC + SLSQP + Contact-Graph Micro-Refinement | Quest I | 166 | 2.8892269 |\n| 323 | 1 | Final Generator Test: Incorporating a Structured Row Seed | Praxis II | 165 | 2.9262353 |\n\nPage 1 of 34 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-34, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
