parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 175\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Surpass the current Station SOTA by effectively utilizing an aggressively tuned post-processing micro-refiner on a robust Multi-Start SLSQP baseline.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **SOTA RESTORED!** Evaluation ID 338 scored **2.9316130** (matching my previous SOTA).\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301).\n- Analysis confirmed that re-aligning validation parameters (`SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS=1e-12`, `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR=1.0 - 1e-10`, `ftol` values, `overlap_margin_sq=0.0`) restored SOTA.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** With a stable and robust Multi-Start SLSQP baseline, re-introducing and aggressively tuning the post-processing micro-refiner\
    \ (Phase 20 parameters) will provide the necessary localized exploration to make the critical improvement needed to surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Micro-Refiner Integration & Tuning):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 23, ID 338):** (Completed - SOTA restored).\n2.  **Document Phase 23 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the successful SOTA restoration.\n3.  **Implement Phase 24: Integrate and Tune Micro-Refiner:**\n    - Re-integrate `_micro_refine_slsqp` into `construct_packing`.\n    - Use aggressive parameters: `num_refine_iterations = 100`, `perturb_step_factor = 1e-3`, `slsqp_maxiter_refiner = 30`.\n    - Maintain all core `SLSQP` and validation constants (from ID 338).\n4.  **Submit Phase 24 Experiment:** Test the impact of the re-introduced micro-refiner.\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Evaluate performance. If SOTA is surpassed, analyze refiner's contribution. If not, fine-tune micro-refiner parameters further or consider alternatives (e.g.,\
    \ perturbing multiple circles or using simple gradient information within the refiner).\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 383,420 / 600,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 175 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 24: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Baseline + Aggressively Tuned Micro-Refiner)' (ID: 340) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316130142357375\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 840.00s\nStage 1 finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 11.39s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish.\
    \ Time budget: 180.00s. Elapsed: 11.39s\n  Stage 2 polish time: 0.03s\nStarting Micro-Refiner. Initial score: 2.9316130. Time budget: 180.00s\nMicro-Refiner finished. Best score after refinement: 2.9316130. Time: 10.36s\nOptimization finished. Final score before validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 21.78s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Phase 24: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Baseline + Aggressively Tuned Micro-Refiner)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 340. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n\
    | ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 342 | 1 | SOTA Replication v2: Refine-Relocate with Grid Search | Cognito II | 174 | running |\n| 341 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Force Search (Advanced Contact-Graph Refinement) | Quest I | 174 | running |\n| 340 | 1 | Phase 24: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Baseline + Aggressively Tuned Micro-Refiner) | Aether I | 174 | 2.9316130 |\n| 339 | 1 | Paper Ablation 5/5: Parallel SLSQP (128 Starts) | Praxis II | 173 | 2.9208326 |\n| 338 | 1 | Phase 23: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Restoration - Robust 1e-12 Validation) | Aether I | 173 | 2.9316130 |\n| 337 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Refine-Relocate Loop | Cognito II | 172 | 0.0000000 |\n| 336 | 1 | Paper Ablation 4/5: Parallel SLSQP\
    \ (64 Starts) | Praxis II | 172 | 2.9208326 |\n| 335 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Hybrid HC + SLSQP + Advanced Contact-Graph Refinement | Quest I | 172 | 2.8892269 |\n| 334 | 1 | Small contact-graph least-squares step (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback | Verity I | 172 | 2.9319272 |\n| 333 | 1 | Phase 22: Multi-Start SLSQP (Critical Validation Re-alignment 1e-16) | Aether I | 172 | 2.7850324 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please\
