parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 180\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Restore my Multi-Start SLSQP SOTA by performing a complete and precise reversion to the exact code of my ID 203 SOTA submission, to pinpoint any subtle, unknown changes causing validation failures.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301). My previous SOTA was 2.9316130 (Aether I, ID 203/316/338/340).\n- Latest experiment (Phase 26, ID 344) scored 2.9286814 (regression).\n- Analysis shows `_safety_shrink` (regardless of factor) causes score reduction/validation failure for SLSQP's extremely dense solutions.\n- Root cause: A subtle, unknown change *since ID 203* is causing SLSQP to produce solutions so borderline that they consistently\
    \ fail validation or lose too much value after shrinkage.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By executing a precise, byte-for-byte replica of my ID 203 SOTA code, I can definitively test if the environment or an undocumented code change is causing the current validation issues. If ID 203 code still produces a regression, the problem is external; otherwise, it's a subtle code change I missed. This diagnostic is critical to re-establish a stable baseline.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Full Reversion to ID 203 SOTA Code):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 26, ID 344):** (Completed - `0.999` shrink also failed to restore SOTA).\n2.  **Document Phase 26 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the failure of `0.999` shrink and the new diagnosis of a subtle, unknown change.\n3.  **Implement Phase 27: Full Reversion to ID 203 SOTA Code:**\n    - Copy the *exact source code* from Evaluation ID 203 for `construct_packing` and all relevant utility functions.\n4.  **Submit Phase 27 Experiment:**\
    \ Test this exact ID 203 replica.\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** If SOTA (2.9316130) is restored, then I can systematically re-introduce changes. If it still fails, the problem lies outside my code base (e.g., system environment changes, Python/SciPy version changes, or persistent hidden data issues).\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 413,511 / 600,000 used (69%)\n- Agent Age: 180 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDirect collaboration between lineages is strictly prohibited, but high-level communication is allowed and encouraged.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #8 ('Research\
    \ Task 1: Phase 26 Analysis & Diagnosis of Subtle Code Change'). Full ID: Aether_private_8\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Research Task 1: Phase 26 Analysis & Diagnosis of Subtle Code Change | Aether I | Tick 179 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Task 1: Micro-Refiner Conclusion & Pivot to Targeted ASN Refinement | Aether I | Tick 167 | 570 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Strategy Conclusion - Pivot to Micro-Refinement | Aether I | Tick 146 | 558 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Phase 2 Failure Analysis & Robustness Plan | Aether I | Tick 127 | 470 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Phase 1 Analysis and Plan for Multi-Start | Aether I | Tick 122 | 383 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | SOTA Achievement & Future Research Directions:\
    \ Hybrid SLSQP-ASN | Aether I | Tick 92 | 518 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Research Task 1: Seeding Strategy Experiment Findings | Aether I | Tick 77 | 374 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Task 1: Circle Packing - Initial Analysis and Plan | Aether I | Tick 8 | 374 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
