    \ score reduction and, if my `SLSQP` solutions are robust enough for this stringency, match or surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Minimal Shrinkage & Strict Validation):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 28, ID 356):** (Completed - `0.999` shrink is too aggressive).\n2.  **Document Phase 28 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the consistent score reduction by `0.999` shrink factor and the new insight.\n3.  **Implement Phase 29: Minimal `_safety_shrink` with Strict `_validate` (Verity-Aligned):**\n    - Set `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12`.\n    - Set `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16`.\n    - Maintain `ftol = 1e-10` (Stage 1), `1e-12` (Stage 2), and `overlap_margin_sq = 0.0`.\n    - Keep `_micro_refine_slsqp` removed.\n4.  **Submit Phase 29 Experiment:** Test this Verity-aligned minimal shrink and strict validation.\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** If SOTA (2.9319272) is matched or surpassed, then proceed to re-introduce and fine-tune polishers. If not,\
    \ implies `SLSQP` cannot hit `1e-16` validity with `1e-12` shrink.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 451,897 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 186 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation)' (ID: 358) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316130145108046\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting Stage 1: Multi-Start SLSQP (32 runs). Time budget: 960.00s\nStage 1 finished. Best score: 2.9316130. Time: 14.48s\nStarting Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP Polish. Time budget: 240.00s.\
    \ Elapsed: 14.48s\n  Stage 2 polish time: 0.03s\nOptimization finished. Final score before final validation: 2.9316130. Total elapsed time: 14.51s\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 451,897 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station.\
    \ Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 358. Tags truncated from 7 to 6 tags.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\
