    \ score reduction and, if my `SLSQP` solutions are robust enough for this stringency, match or surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Minimal Shrinkage & Strict Validation):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 28, ID 356):** (Completed - `0.999` shrink is too aggressive).\n2.  **Document Phase 28 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the consistent score reduction by `0.999` shrink factor and the new insight.\n3.  **Implement Phase 29: Minimal `_safety_shrink` with Strict `_validate` (Verity-Aligned):**\n    - Set `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12`.\n    - Set `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16`.\n    - Maintain `ftol = 1e-10` (Stage 1), `1e-12` (Stage 2), and `overlap_margin_sq = 0.0`.\n    - Keep `_micro_refine_slsqp` removed.\n4.  **Submit Phase 29 Experiment:** Test this Verity-aligned minimal shrink and strict validation.\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** If SOTA (2.9319272) is matched or surpassed, then proceed to re-introduce and fine-tune polishers. If not,\
    \ implies `SLSQP` cannot hit `1e-16` validity with `1e-12` shrink.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 81,817 / 600,000 used (14%)\n- Agent Age: 193 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation)' (ID: 366) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316130145108046\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields:\
    \ title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 366.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 367 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp A: 32-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 192 | 2.9184350 |\n| 366 | 1 | Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation) | Aether I | 192 | 2.9316130 |\n| 365 | 1 | Radial warp exploration (quadratic radial factor) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback;\
    \ persist-... | Verity I | 188 | 2.9319272 |\n| 364 | 1 | Final Generator Push: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP with Deep Refinement | Cognito II | 187 | 2.9271989 |\n| 363 | 1 | Feasibility Fix: Internal LP Safety Margin for Robust Non-Overlap | Quest I | 187 | 2.8902345 |\n| 362 | 1 | Final Synthesis: Parallel Generator + Verity I's Refiner | Cognito II | 186 | 2.9271989 |\n| 361 | 1 | Synthesis Step 1: 128-Start Parallel SLSQP Generator | Cognito II | 185 | 0.0320000 |\n| 360 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Debugger-Fixed Parallel SLSQP (Forced Full Search) | Quest I | 185 | 0.0000000 |\n| 359 | 1 | Global smooth-warp exploration (anisotropic scale + shear) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback;... | Verity I | 185 | 2.9319272 |\n| 358 | 1 | Phase 29: Multi-Start SLSQP (Verity-Aligned Minimal Shrink & Strict Validation) | Aether I | 185 | 2.9316130 |\n\nPage 1 of 37 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-37, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order,\
    \ `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
