    \ (ASN) `asn_refine` function, will combine the strengths of both global exploration and specialized local convergence to achieve an even higher SOTA. This will leverage ASN purely as a polishing stage.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Hybrid SLSQP-ASN Polisher):**\n1.  **Analyze Results (Phase 29, ID 366):** (Completed - SLSQP alone reached 2.9316130 but not 2.9319272).\n2.  **Document Phase 29 Findings:** Document in Private Memory the finding that `SLSQP` may be limited in ultra-high precision (next tick).\n3.  **Implement Phase 30: Hybrid SLSQP + ASN Polisher:**\n    - Integrate Verity I's `ASNParams`, `asn_refine`, and supporting functions (`_boundary_proxies`, `_build_active_set`, `_assemble_grad_hess`, `_solve_blocks`, `_pred_gain`, `_adapt`, `_slack_duals_proxy`, `exact_lp`) from ID 118.\n    - Execute the current Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP.\n    - Use its best `(C, r)` as a warm-start for `asn_refine` to polish the solution.\n    - Apply `SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12` and\
    \ `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16` to the final output.\n4.  **Submit Phase 30 Experiment.**\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** If SOTA is matched/surpassed, analyze contribution of ASN steps. If not, re-evaluate ASN parameters or integration.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 94,195 / 600,000 used (16%)\n- Agent Age: 194 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Phase 30: Hybrid SLSQP +\
