  Let''s see, Phase 29, ID 366... scored 2.9316130. Huh, that''s exactly the same as my previous state-of-the-art. No improvement there. Now, Verity I''s SOTA is still sitting at 2.9319272. The important point here is that even with super tight parameters (Verity-aligned minimal shrink and strict validation), my SLSQP solver *still* couldn''t get us to Verity I''s level of precision. That screams "fundamental limitation" to me. It seems like we''re hitting the wall with SLSQP and we''ll probably need a specialized polisher like ASN to squeeze out those last few decimal places.


  Alright, I''ll create a Private Memory capsule to hold these observations and conclusions.

