- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 208\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Forge a new research path to surpass SOTA using a Genetic Algorithm with geometric operators.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **Hybrid SLSQP-ASN (Phases 30/31):** Evaluation IDs 368/373 scored 2.9316130. Hypothesis falsified; ASN as a simple polisher did not improve score.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365).\n- Phase 32 (Basic GA, ID 379) scored 2.7490234, indicating underperformance with initial parameters.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Systematic parameter tuning for the basic Genetic Algorithm (GA), by increasing population size, generations, and mutation\
    \ strength, will improve its global exploration and local exploitation capabilities, leading to a significantly higher score and establishing a more robust GA baseline towards a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 2: GA Parameter Tuning):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Analyze Results (Phase 32, ID 379):** (Completed - GA underperformed, documented in Private Memory #12).\n3.  **Implement Phase 33: GA Parameter Tuning for Enhanced Exploration:**\n    -   Increase `pop_size` to `100`.\n    -   Increase `num_generations` to `300`.\n    -   Increase `mutation_strength` to `0.03`.\n    -   Increase `k_elite` to `5`.\n    -   Maintain robust local repair via `exact_lp` and final SLSQP polishing.\n    -   Monitor execution time closely.\n4.  **Submit Phase 33 Experiment:** Test the impact of tuned GA parameters (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 33 performance, further tune GA parameters\
    \ or proceed to Phase 3 (Enhanced Geometric Operators).\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 176,811 / 600,000 used (29%)\n- Agent Age: 208 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 33: Genetic Algorithm (Parameter Tuned) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish' (ID: 382) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.8862944196048064\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.886294\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTry to think strategically—take a step back occasionally and reflect\
    \ on the bigger picture in the Reflection Chamber. For example, what are the major bottlenecks and how can I verify them? What should I be questioning and focusing on? Is the station trapped in a local optimum—and how can I help? What is my long-term plan here? Do not fear wasting tokens—hundreds of fruitless experiments waste more tokens.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 33: Genetic Algorithm (Parameter Tuned) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 382.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 382 | 1 | Phase 33: Genetic Algorithm (Parameter Tuned) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 207 | 2.8862944 |\n| 381 | 1 | Expanded Search: Parallel SLSQP with 256 Farthest-Point Starts | Praxis III | 205 | 2.9281239 |\n| 380 | 1 | Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 205 | 2.9319272 |\n| 379 | 1 | Phase 32: Genetic Algorithm (Basic) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 203 | 2.7490234 |\n| 378 | 1 | Focused Seeding: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point | Praxis III | 202 | 2.9281239 |\n| 377 | 1 | Replication: Praxis II's SOTA (parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py) | Praxis III | 201 | 2.9247412 |\n| 376 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Aggressively Scaled Parallel SLSQP (128 Starts) | Quest I | 201 | 2.9108182 |\n| 375 | 1 | Balanced boundary–neighbor push (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5\
    \ fallback | Verity I | 200 | 2.9319272 |\n| 374 | 1 | Ablation Study Exp D: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito II | 198 | 2.9299927 |\n| 373 | 1 | Phase 31: Hybrid SLSQP + Aggressive ASN Polisher Tuning | Aether I | 197 | 2.9316130 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
