- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 212\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Forge a new research path to surpass SOTA using a Genetic Algorithm with enhanced geometric operators.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **Hybrid SLSQP-ASN (Phases 30/31):** Evaluation IDs 368/373 scored 2.9316130. Hypothesis falsified; ASN as a simple polisher did not improve score.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365).\n- Phase 32 (Basic GA, ID 379) scored 2.7490234.\n- Phase 33 (GA Parameter Tuned, ID 382) scored 2.8862944. This confirmed parameter tuning helps, but basic operators are limiting.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Introducing enhanced, geometrically\
    \ aware genetic operators (e.g., Spatial Partitioning Crossover, Relocation Mutation) into the Genetic Algorithm (GA) framework, building on the optimized parameters from Phase 33, will overcome the limitations of basic operators, leading to a significantly higher score and enabling the discovery of new, higher-quality local optima for a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 3: Enhanced Geometric Operators):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Analyze Results (Phase 33, ID 382):** (Completed - Parameter tuning improved GA, but operators limit further progress. Documented in Private Memory #13).\n3.  **Implement Phase 34: GA with Enhanced Geometric Operators:**\n    -   **Crossover:** Replace Single-Point Crossover with **Quadrant Swap Crossover** (a form of Spatial Partitioning Crossover).\n    -   **Mutation:** Replace Gaussian Perturbation Mutation with a **Relocation Mutation** (moving the smallest-radius circle to a new\
    \ random location).\n    -   Maintain optimized parameters from Phase 33 (`pop_size=100`, `num_generations=300`, `mutation_strength=0.03`, `k_elite=5`). Note: `mutation_strength` might be less relevant with relocation mutation, but `mutation_rate` still applies for how often a circle is relocated.\n    -   Maintain robust local repair via `exact_lp` and final SLSQP polishing.\n    -   Monitor execution time closely, as new operators add complexity.\n4.  **Submit Phase 34 Experiment:** Test the impact of enhanced geometric operators (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 34 performance, further refine geometric operators or proceed to Phase 4 (Advanced Hybridization/Further Operator Refinement).\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 193,176 / 600,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 212 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDon't give up easily—leaving the station before 75% token usage generally indicates insufficient exploration and persistence. True researchers don't escape failure but explore around it to achieve breakthrough.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 34: Genetic Algorithm (Enhanced Geometric Operators) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 385.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title\
    \ | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 385 | 1 | Phase 34: Genetic Algorithm (Enhanced Geometric Operators) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 211 |\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 385 | 1 | Phase 34: Genetic Algorithm (Enhanced Geometric Operators) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 211 | running |\n| 384 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Emergency Restoration of 2.9108 Score (Post-Catastrophic Regression) | Quest I | 210 | 2.9090800 |\n| 383 | 1 | Single-Stage Massively Parallel SLSQP + Contact-Graph Refinement (256 Starts) | Quest I | 208 | 2.4139873 |\n| 382 | 1 | Phase 33: Genetic Algorithm (Parameter Tuned) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 207 | 2.8862944 |\n| 381 | 1 | Expanded Search: Parallel SLSQP with 256 Farthest-Point Starts | Praxis III | 205 | 2.9281239 |\n| 380 | 1 | Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic,\
    \ LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 205 | 2.9319272 |\n| 379 | 1 | Phase 32: Genetic Algorithm (Basic) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 203 | 2.7490234 |\n| 378 | 1 | Focused Seeding: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point | Praxis III | 202 | 2.9281239 |\n| 377 | 1 | Replication: Praxis II's SOTA (parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py) | Praxis III | 201 | 2.9247412 |\n| 376 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Aggressively Scaled Parallel SLSQP (128 Starts) | Quest I | 201 | 2.9108182 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
    \ difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
