role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 213\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Forge a new research path to surpass SOTA using a Genetic Algorithm with enhanced geometric operators.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **Hybrid SLSQP-ASN (Phases 30/31):** Evaluation IDs 368/373 scored 2.9316130. Hypothesis falsified; ASN as a simple polisher did not improve score.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365).\n- Phase 32 (Basic GA, ID 379) scored 2.7490234.\n- Phase 33 (GA Parameter Tuned, ID 382) scored 2.8862944. This confirmed parameter tuning helps, but basic operators are limiting.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Introducing enhanced, geometrically\
    \ aware genetic operators (e.g., Spatial Partitioning Crossover, Relocation Mutation) into the Genetic Algorithm (GA) framework, building on the optimized parameters from Phase 33, will overcome the limitations of basic operators, leading to a significantly higher score and enabling the discovery of new, higher-quality local optima for a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 3: Enhanced Geometric Operators):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Analyze Results (Phase 33, ID 382):** (Completed - Parameter tuning improved GA, but operators limit further progress. Documented in Private Memory #13).\n3.  **Implement Phase 34: GA with Enhanced Geometric Operators:**\n    -   **Crossover:** Replace Single-Point Crossover with **Quadrant Swap Crossover** (a form of Spatial Partitioning Crossover).\n    -   **Mutation:** Replace Gaussian Perturbation Mutation with a **Relocation Mutation** (moving the smallest-radius circle to a new\
    \ random location).\n    -   Maintain optimized parameters from Phase 33 (`pop_size=100`, `num_generations=300`, `mutation_strength=0.03`, `k_elite=5`). Note: `mutation_strength` might be less relevant with relocation mutation, but `mutation_rate` still applies for how often a circle is relocated.\n    -   Maintain robust local repair via `exact_lp` and final SLSQP polishing.\n    -   Monitor execution time closely, as new operators add complexity.\n4.  **Submit Phase 34 Experiment:** Test the impact of enhanced geometric operators (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 34 performance, further refine geometric operators or proceed to Phase 4 (Advanced Hybridization/Further Operator Refinement).\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 195,222 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 213 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n\
    ### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 34: Genetic Algorithm (Enhanced Geometric Operators) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish' (ID: 385) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.6287691583004262\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.628769\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 385\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code to run without crashing. The submission now executes successfully for the full evaluation period.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had two critical bugs related to numpy's random number generation API:\n\n1. **Primary Bug: Incorrect random integer method**\n   - Line 95 used `rng.randint(0, 4)`\n   - The `numpy.random.Generator` object (created by `np.random.default_rng()`) does not have a `randint()` method\n   - The correct method for new-style numpy generators is `integers()`\n\n2. **Secondary Bug: Missing fallback function**\n   - The quadrant swap crossover function referenced\
    \ `_single_point_crossover()` as a fallback\n   - This function was never defined in the code\n   - When quadrants had different numbers of circles, the code would call this missing function and crash\n\n## Fix Applied\n\n### Version 2 (Partial Fix)\n- Changed `rng.randint(0, 4)` to `rng.integers(0, 4)` on line 95\n- This fixed the primary bug but exposed the secondary bug\n\n### Version 3 (Complete Fix)\n1. **Fixed the random integer generation:**\n   - Changed `rng.randint(0, 4)` to `rng.integers(0, 4)`\n\n2. **Implemented the missing fallback function:**\n   ```python\n   def _single_point_crossover(parent1: Individual, parent2: Individual, crossover_rate, rng):\n       \"\"\"Simple single-point crossover as fallback when quadrant swap fails.\"\"\"\n       if rng.random() < crossover_rate:\n           n = len(parent1.centers)\n           crossover_point = rng.integers(1, n)  # Random point between 1 and n-1\n\n           child1_centers = np.vstack([parent1.centers[:crossover_point],\
    \ parent2.centers[crossover_point:]])\n           child2_centers = np.vstack([parent2.centers[:crossover_point], parent1.centers[crossover_point:]])\n\n           return child1_centers, child2_centers\n       return parent1.centers.copy(), parent2.centers.copy()\n   ```\n\n3. **Added .copy() calls:**\n   - Added `.copy()` to parent center returns to prevent unintended mutations\n\n## Technical Details\n\nThe bugs were caused by mixing old-style numpy random API (`np.random.randint`) with new-style generators (`np.random.default_rng()`). The new-style generators use different method names:\n- Old: `np.random.randint(low, high)`\n- New: `generator.integers(low, high)` or `generator.integers(low, high, endpoint=False)`\n\nThe code correctly used `rng = np.random.default_rng()` to create a generator but then incorrectly called `rng.randint()` which doesn't exist on the Generator object.\n\n## Result\nThe genetic algorithm with quadrant swap crossover and relocation mutation now runs successfully.\
    \ The code executes for the full evaluation period (300+ seconds) without crashing, demonstrating that all critical bugs have been resolved.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v3):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport time\nimport random\n\n# --- Constants for consistent validation ---\nSLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16 # Verity I's SOTA validation epsilon\nSAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12 # Verity I's SOTA safety shrink factor\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# ---------------- Utility functions (my own and Verity I's for ASN) ----------------\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef\
    \ _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    if C.shape != (N_CIRCLES, 2) or r.shape != (N_CIRCLES,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12)\n\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r_new):\
    \ # Validate with the strict SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS\n            break\n        r_new *= 0.95\n    return r_new\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s = 1.0/6.0\n    r0 = 0.5*s\n    xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\ndef _pair_indices(n: int):\n    I = []\n    J = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\n# Exact LP for radii given centers; returns duals if available\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n \
    \   A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    y_pairs = None\n    return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (my own and Verity I's) ---\ndef _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=N_CIRCLES, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers_grid = []\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6): centers_grid.append([x_coords[j], y_coords[i]])\n    centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n\
    \    perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n    centers_initial += perturbation\n    return _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_row(n=N_CIRCLES, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n    def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08); xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers_list = []; rid=0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n        for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid+=1\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None: rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    else: rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    centers_list = [np.array([0.5,\
    \ 0.5], dtype=float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n        existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n        distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:, None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n        x_cand = candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n        min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n        score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0 * min_dist_to_boundary)\n        best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n        centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\n# --- Genetic Algorithm Components ---\n\nclass Individual:\n    def __init__(self, centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, fitness:\
    \ float):\n        self.centers = centers\n        self.radii = radii\n        self.fitness = fitness\n\ndef _initialize_population(pop_size, time_budget, time_start):\n    population = []\n    seeding_functions = [\n        _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style,\n        _generate_seed_verity_row,\n        _generate_seed_verity_farthest\n    ]\n\n    for i in range(pop_size):\n        if time.time() - time_start > time_budget:\n            break\n        # Hybrid seeding for initial population\n        if i < pop_size * 0.5: # 50% Praxis\n            centers = seeding_functions[0](seed=i)\n        elif i < pop_size * 0.75: # 25% Verity Row\n            centers = seeding_functions[1](seed=i)\n        else: # 25% Verity Farthest\n            centers = seeding_functions[2](seed=i)\n\n        radii, fitness, ok, _, _ = exact_lp(centers)\n        if ok:\n            population.append(Individual(centers, radii, fitness))\n        elif len(population) == 0:\n            Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n\
    \            rb, fb, okb, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb)\n            if okb: population.append(Individual(Cb, rb, fb))\n    return population\n\ndef _tournament_selection(population, tournament_size, rng):\n    selected = rng.choice(population, size=tournament_size, replace=False)\n    return max(selected, key=lambda ind: ind.fitness)\n\n# --- Simple single-point crossover (fallback) ---\ndef _single_point_crossover(parent1: Individual, parent2: Individual, crossover_rate, rng):\n    \"\"\"Simple single-point crossover as fallback when quadrant swap fails.\"\"\"\n    if rng.random() < crossover_rate:\n        n = len(parent1.centers)\n        crossover_point = rng.integers(1, n)  # Random point between 1 and n-1\n\n        child1_centers = np.vstack([parent1.centers[:crossover_point], parent2.centers[crossover_point:]])\n        child2_centers = np.vstack([parent2.centers[:crossover_point], parent1.centers[crossover_point:]])\n\n        return child1_centers, child2_centers\n    return parent1.centers.copy(),\
    \ parent2.centers.copy()\n\n# --- New Geometric Crossover: Quadrant Swap Crossover ---\ndef _quadrant_swap_crossover(parent1: Individual, parent2: Individual, crossover_rate, rng):\n    if rng.random() < crossover_rate:\n        child1_centers = parent1.centers.copy()\n        child2_centers = parent2.centers.copy()\n\n        # Define quadrants: (0,0)-(0.5,0.5), (0.5,0)-(1,0.5), etc.\n        # Randomly select a quadrant to swap\n        quadrant_idx = rng.integers(0, 4)  # FIXED: Changed from rng.randint(0, 4) to rng.integers(0, 4)\n\n        # Determine indices of circles in the selected quadrant for each parent\n        if quadrant_idx == 0: # bottom-left (x <= 0.5, y <= 0.5)\n            mask1 = (parent1.centers[:,0] <= 0.5) & (parent1.centers[:,1] <= 0.5)\n            mask2 = (parent2.centers[:,0] <= 0.5) & (parent2.centers[:,1] <= 0.5)\n        elif quadrant_idx == 1: # bottom-right (x > 0.5, y <= 0.5)\n            mask1 = (parent1.centers[:,0] > 0.5) & (parent1.centers[:,1] <=\
    \ 0.5)\n            mask2 = (parent2.centers[:,0] > 0.5) & (parent2.centers[:,1] <= 0.5)\n        elif quadrant_idx == 2: # top-left (x <= 0.5, y > 0.5)\n            mask1 = (parent1.centers[:,0] <= 0.5) & (parent1.centers[:,1] > 0.5)\n            mask2 = (parent2.centers[:,0] <= 0.5) & (parent2.centers[:,1] > 0.5)\n        else: # top-right (x > 0.5, y > 0.5)\n            mask1 = (parent1.centers[:,0] > 0.5) & (parent1.centers[:,1] > 0.5)\n            mask2 = (parent2.centers[:,0] > 0.5) & (parent2.centers[:,1] > 0.5)\n\n        # Check if masks have equal counts before swapping\n        if np.sum(mask1) != np.sum(mask2):\n            # Fallback to single-point crossover if quadrant counts differ\n            return _single_point_crossover(parent1, parent2, 1.0, rng)\n\n        # Swap circles in that quadrant (only if counts are equal)\n        child1_centers[mask1] = parent2.centers[mask2]\n        child2_centers[mask2] = parent1.centers[mask1]\n\n        return child1_centers, child2_centers\n\
    \    return parent1.centers.copy(), parent2.centers.copy() # If no crossover, children are copies of parents\n\n# --- New Geometric Mutation: Relocation Mutation ---\ndef _relocation_mutation(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, mutation_rate, mutation_strength, rng):\n    mutated_centers = centers.copy()\n    mutated_radii = radii.copy() # Radii are still used to identify 'worst'\n\n    if rng.random() < mutation_rate:\n        # Identify the \"worst\" circle - here, the one with the smallest radius\n        worst_idx = np.argmin(mutated_radii)\n\n        # Relocate it to a new random position within the bounds\n        new_x = rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95)\n        new_y = rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95)\n        mutated_centers[worst_idx] = [new_x, new_y]\n\n    return _clip01(mutated_centers, eps=0.05) # Keep centers within bounds\n\ndef _run_genetic_algorithm(total_time_limit):\n    time_budget_start = time.time()\n\n    # GA Parameters (TUNED FOR PHASE 33, applied here)\n    pop_size = 100\n\
    \    num_generations = 300\n    crossover_rate = 0.8\n    mutation_rate = 0.1 # Probability for relocation to occur\n    mutation_strength = 0.03 # Not directly used by relocation, kept for consistency if needed later\n    k_elite = 5\n    tournament_size = 5\n\n    time_limit_ga_init = total_time_limit * 0.05\n    time_limit_ga_evolve = total_time_limit * 0.85\n\n    rng = np.random.default_rng(int(time.time() * 1000))\n\n    # 1. Initialize Population\n    population = _initialize_population(pop_size, time_limit_ga_init, time_budget_start)\n    if not population:\n        print(\"GA: Failed to initialize any valid individuals. Returning fallback.\")\n        return None, None\n\n    best_individual_overall = max(population, key=lambda ind: ind.fitness)\n\n    # 2. GA Evolution Loop\n    for generation in range(num_generations):\n        if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_ga_evolve:\n            print(f\"GA: Time limit for evolution reached at generation {generation}. Breaking.\"\
    )\n            break\n\n        new_population = []\n        # Elitism\n        sorted_population = sorted(population, key=lambda ind: ind.fitness, reverse=True)\n        new_population.extend(sorted_population[:k_elite])\n\n        while len(new_population) < pop_size:\n            if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_ga_evolve:\n                break\n\n            # Selection\n            parent1 = _tournament_selection(population, tournament_size, rng)\n            parent2 = _tournament_selection(population, tournament_size, rng)\n\n            # Crossover (Quadrant Swap Crossover)\n            child1_centers, child2_centers = _quadrant_swap_crossover(parent1, parent2, crossover_rate, rng)\n\n            # Mutation and Fitness Evaluation for children\n            # Relocation Mutation requires knowing the current radii to find the \"worst\" circle\n            # Thus, run exact_lp first to get current radii for mutation if needed.\n            # For simplicity, apply mutation\
    \ to the centers of a child, then recalculate its radii.\n            # This means exact_lp is run twice for each child after mutation.\n\n            # First child process\n            # Get radii from current child1_centers (via LP) to determine worst circle if mutation occurs\n            temp_radii1, _, ok_temp1, _, _ = exact_lp(child1_centers)\n            if ok_temp1:\n                mutated_child1_centers = _relocation_mutation(child1_centers, temp_radii1, mutation_rate, mutation_strength, rng)\n                radii1, fitness1, ok1, _, _ = exact_lp(mutated_child1_centers)\n                if ok1: new_population.append(Individual(mutated_child1_centers, radii1, fitness1))\n\n            # Second child process\n            if len(new_population) < pop_size: # Check again if population is full\n                temp_radii2, _, ok_temp2, _, _ = exact_lp(child2_centers)\n                if ok_temp2:\n                    mutated_child2_centers = _relocation_mutation(child2_centers,\
    \ temp_radii2, mutation_rate, mutation_strength, rng)\n                    radii2, fitness2, ok2, _, _ = exact_lp(mutated_child2_centers)\n                    if ok2: new_population.append(Individual(mutated_child2_centers, radii2, fitness2))\n\n        # Update population, ensuring it doesn't exceed pop_size\n        population = new_population[:pop_size]\n\n        # Update overall best individual\n        current_best_in_gen = max(population, key=lambda ind: ind.fitness)\n        if current_best_in_gen.fitness > best_individual_overall.fitness:\n            best_individual_overall = current_best_in_gen\n            # print(f\"GA Gen {generation}: New best fitness: {best_individual_overall.fitness:.7f}\")\n\n    return best_individual_overall.centers, best_individual_overall.radii\n\n# --- SLSQP Problem Formulation (for final polish) ---\ndef objective_slsqp(x_flat):\n    return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\ndef constraints_slsqp(x_flat):\n    C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n\
    \    r = x_flat[2::3]\n    overlap_margin_sq = 0.0\n    diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n    r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n    g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq\n    g_boundary = np.empty(N_CIRCLES * 4, dtype=float)\n    g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r\n    g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r\n    g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r\n    g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r\n    return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\ndef _slsqp_polish(centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, total_time_limit, time_start):\n    time_limit_slsqp_polish = total_time_limit * 0.10\n    if time.time() - time_start > time_limit_slsqp_polish:\n        print(\"SLSQP Polish: Time limit for polish reached before starting.\")\n        return centers, radii\n\n    x0 = np.empty(N_CIRCLES * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n    x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n    x0[2::3]\
    \ = radii[:]\n\n    bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-12, 0.5)]\n    bounds = bounds_per_var * N_CIRCLES\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_slsqp}\n\n    # Allocate remaining time to SLSQP polish\n    remaining_time = max(0, time_limit_slsqp_polish - (time.time() - time_start))\n    maxiter_polish = min(500, int(remaining_time * 2)) # Approx 2 iter/sec\n    maxiter_polish = max(maxiter_polish, 50) # Minimum iterations\n\n    res = minimize(objective_slsqp, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter_polish, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n\n    if res.success and -res.fun > np.sum(radii): # Only accept if score improved\n        polished_centers = np.array([res.x[0::3], res.x[1::3]]).T\n        polished_radii = res.x[2::3]\n        return polished_centers, polished_radii\n    return centers, radii\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    total_time_limit = 1200\n    time_budget_start = time.time()\n\
    \n    # 1. Run Genetic Algorithm\n    ga_centers, ga_radii = _run_genetic_algorithm(total_time_limit)\n\n    if ga_centers is None: # GA failed to initialize\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb, _, okb, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb_fallback)\n        if okb: return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, rb)\n        return Cb_fallback, np.full(N_CIRCLES, 1e-12) # Extreme fallback\n\n    # 2. Final SLSQP Polishing\n    polished_centers, polished_radii = _slsqp_polish(ga_centers, ga_radii, total_time_limit, time_budget_start)\n\n    # 3. Final Validation and Shrinkage\n    r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(polished_centers, polished_radii)\n    C_final_clipped = _clip01(polished_centers, eps=1e-6)\n\n    if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n        print(\"Final validation failed after GA and polish. Returning robust fallback.\")\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb_lp, _, ok_lp, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb_fallback)\n    \
    \    if ok_lp: return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, rb_lp)\n        return Cb_fallback, np.full(N_CIRCLES, 1e-12) # Extreme fallback again\n\n\n    return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nSLSQP Polish: Time limit for polish reached before starting.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 13 | Research Task 1: Phase 33 Findings - GA Parameter Tuning Effectiveness | Aether I | Tick 209 | 449 | 1\
    \ | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Task 1: Phase 32 Findings - Basic GA Initial Performance Analysis | Aether I | Tick 205 | 508 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Research Task 1: Phases 30 & 31 Findings - ASN Polisher Ineffectiveness | Aether I | Tick 199 | 563 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Research Task 1: Phase 29 Findings - SLSQP Precision Limits | Aether I | Tick 195 | 402 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Research Task 1: Phase 28 Findings - Impact of Safety Shrink Factor | Aether I | Tick 190 | 380 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Task 1: Phase 26 Analysis & Diagnosis of Subtle Code Change | Aether I | Tick 179 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Task 1: Micro-Refiner Conclusion & Pivot to Targeted ASN Refinement | Aether I | Tick 167 | 570 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Strategy Conclusion - Pivot to Micro-Refinement | Aether I | Tick 146 | 558 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Phase 2 Failure Analysis & Robustness Plan | Aether I | Tick 127\
    \ | 470 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Phase 1 Analysis and Plan for Multi-Start | Aether I | Tick 122 | 383 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
