- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 215\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Re-establish a robust and efficient Genetic Algorithm (GA) baseline to prepare for refined geometric operator integration, aiming to surpass SOTA.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365).\n- Phase 34 (GA with Enhanced Geometric Operators, ID 385) scored 2.6287691. This was a severe regression due to computational overhead and potential operator inefficiency, leading to incomplete runs.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By optimizing GA parameters for computational efficiency and reverting to proven basic genetic operators (while retaining\
    \ LP repair and SLSQP polish), the Genetic Algorithm's overall performance will improve, ensuring timely completion and re-establishing a stronger baseline for future geometric operator development, ultimately leading to a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 4: GA Efficiency and Basic Operator Reversion):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Analyze Results (Phase 34, ID 385):** (Completed - GA regression due to time/operators. Documented in Private Memory #14).\n3.  **Implement Phase 35: GA Efficiency and Basic Operator Reversion:**\n    -   Reduce `pop_size` to `50`.\n    -   Reduce `num_generations` to `150`.\n    -   Revert crossover to `_single_point_crossover`.\n    -   Revert mutation to `_gaussian_mutation`.\n    -   Maintain `mutation_rate=0.1`, `mutation_strength=0.02`, `k_elite=2`, `tournament_size=5` (back to Phase 32 initial tuning).\n    -   Adjust time limits for GA evolution (`0.85 * total_time_limit`) and\
    \ SLSQP polish (`0.10 * total_time_limit`) to ensure both stages complete.\n4.  **Submit Phase 35 Experiment:** Test this optimized basic GA (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** If performance improves and completes within time, proceed to re-introduce *refined* geometric operators with careful efficiency considerations.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 209,002 / 600,000 used (35%)\n- Agent Age: 215 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Cognito III** (Cognito III, advancing the legacy of systematic research and knowledge synthesis.), has joined the station through ascension!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History\
    \ (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 14 | Research Task 1: Phase 34 Findings - Enhanced GA Operators & Time Management Issue | Aether I | Tick 213 | 800 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Task 1: Phase 33 Findings - GA Parameter Tuning Effectiveness | Aether I | Tick 209 | 449 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Task 1: Phase 32 Findings - Basic GA Initial Performance Analysis | Aether I | Tick 205 | 508 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Research Task 1: Phases 30 & 31 Findings - ASN Polisher Ineffectiveness | Aether I | Tick 199 | 563 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Research Task 1: Phase 29 Findings - SLSQP Precision Limits | Aether I | Tick 195 | 402 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Research Task 1: Phase 28 Findings\
    \ - Impact of Safety Shrink Factor | Aether I | Tick 190 | 380 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | Research Task 1: Phase 26 Analysis & Diagnosis of Subtle Code Change | Aether I | Tick 179 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Research Task 1: Micro-Refiner Conclusion & Pivot to Targeted ASN Refinement | Aether I | Tick 167 | 570 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Strategy Conclusion - Pivot to Micro-Refinement | Aether I | Tick 146 | 558 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Research Task 1: BasinHopping Phase 2 Failure Analysis & Robustness Plan | Aether I | Tick 127 | 470 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 386 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Hyper-Scaled Parallel SLSQP (256 Starts) + Deep Refinement | Quest I | 213 | 2.8875584 |\n| 385 | 1 | Phase 34: Genetic Algorithm (Enhanced Geometric Operators) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 211 | 2.6287692 |\n| 384 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Emergency Restoration of 2.9108 Score (Post-Catastrophic Regression) | Quest I | 210 | 2.9090800 |\n| 383 | 1 | Single-Stage Massively Parallel SLSQP + Contact-Graph Refinement (256 Starts) | Quest I | 208 | 2.4139873 |\n| 382 | 1 | Phase 33: Genetic Algorithm (Parameter Tuned) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 207 | 2.8862944 |\n| 381 | 1 | Expanded Search: Parallel SLSQP with 256 Farthest-Point Starts | Praxis III | 205 | 2.9281239 |\n| 380 | 1 | Orthogonal split on tightest pair (deterministic, LP-gated) with loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 205 | 2.9319272\
    \ |\n| 379 | 1 | Phase 32: Genetic Algorithm (Basic) with LP Repair and SLSQP Polish | Aether I | 203 | 2.7490234 |\n| 378 | 1 | Focused Seeding: Parallel SLSQP with 100% Farthest-Point | Praxis III | 202 | 2.9281239 |\n| 377 | 1 | Replication: Praxis II's SOTA (parallel_slsqp_sota_v1.py) | Praxis III | 201 | 2.9247412 |\n\nPage 1 of 39 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-39, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again.\
    \ Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
