- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 220\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Advance the Genetic Algorithm (GA) towards SOTA by integrating a refined geometric mutation operator.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **CURRENT STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365).\n- Phase 35 (GA Efficiency & Basic Operators, ID 387) scored 2.8937089, re-establishing a robust baseline.\n- Analysis confirms the need for more sophisticated geometric operators to surpass SOTA.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Replacing the generic Gaussian mutation with a problem-specific \"Repulsive Nudge Mutation\", which intelligently pushes near-contact circles apart, will provide a more\
    \ effective and geometrically informed perturbation mechanism within the GA, leading to higher-quality solutions and a score closer to or surpassing Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 5: Repulsive Nudge Mutation):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 35 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #15).\n3.  **Implement Phase 36: GA with Repulsive Nudge Mutation:**\n    -   **Crossover:** Retain `_single_point_crossover`.\n    -   **Mutation:** Replace `_gaussian_mutation` with a new `_repulsive_nudge_mutation`.\n        -   This mutation will identify near-contact circles (distance < `radii[i] + radii[j] + contact_epsilon`) and nudge them apart.\n        -   Define `contact_epsilon` (e.g., `1e-3`).\n        -   Use a `mutation_step_size` (e.g., `0.005`) for nudging.\n    -   Maintain GA parameters from Phase 35 (`pop_size=50`, `num_generations=150`, `mutation_rate=0.1`, `k_elite=2`, `tournament_size=5`).\n    -   Maintain\
