    \ Single-Point Crossover, will enable the Genetic Algorithm (GA) to break the current plateau and discover higher-quality solutions, leading to a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 8: Triad Split Mutation):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 38 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #18).\n3.  **Implement Phase 39: GA with Triad Split Mutation & Single-Point Crossover:**\n    -   **Mutation:** Replace `_gaussian_mutation` with a new `_triad_split_mutation`.\n        -   Identify a tight pair `(i*, j*)` (smallest slack) and a nearest third circle `k` (to their midpoint).\n        -   Perform an orthogonal split on `(i*, j*)` and a compensatory nudge on `k` (similar to Verity I's planned \"triad\" motif).\n        -   Define `triad_step_size` (e.g., `0.005`) and `triad_contact_epsilon` (e.g., `1e-3`).\n    -   **Crossover:** Revert to `_single_point_crossover`.\n    -   Maintain efficient GA parameters (`pop_size=50`,\
    \ `num_generations=150`, `mutation_rate=0.1`, `k_elite=2`, `tournament_size=5`).\n    -   Maintain robust local repair via `exact_lp` and final SLSQP polishing.\n    -   Monitor computational cost closely.\n4.  **Submit Phase 39 Experiment:** Test the impact of the Triad Split Mutation (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 39 performance, tune triad parameters, or consider a different coupled operator.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 284,700 / 600,000 used (47%)\n- Agent Age: 233 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\
    \n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 18 | Research Task 1: Phase 38 Findings - Two-Point Crossover Regression & Strategic Re-evaluation | Aether I | Tick 231 | 535 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Research Task 1: Phase 37 Findings - Refined Repulsive Nudge Mutation Failure | Aether I | Tick 225 | 538 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Research Task 1: Phase 36 Findings - Repulsive Nudge Mutation Performance | Aether I | Tick 221 | 551 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Research Task 1: Phase 35 Findings - GA Efficiency & Baseline Re-establishment | Aether I | Tick 217 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Research Task 1: Phase 34 Findings - Enhanced GA Operators & Time Management Issue | Aether I | Tick 213 | 800 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Task 1: Phase 33 Findings - GA Parameter Tuning Effectiveness | Aether I | Tick 209\
    \ | 449 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Task 1: Phase 32 Findings - Basic GA Initial Performance Analysis | Aether I | Tick 205 | 508 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Research Task 1: Phases 30 & 31 Findings - ASN Polisher Ineffectiveness | Aether I | Tick 199 | 563 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Research Task 1: Phase 29 Findings - SLSQP Precision Limits | Aether I | Tick 195 | 402 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 9 | Research Task 1: Phase 28 Findings - Impact of Safety Shrink Factor | Aether I | Tick 190 | 380 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author\
    \ | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 411 | 1 | Experiment 1: Adaptive Parallel Search (1024x60 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 232 | 2.9365262 |\n| 410 | 1 | Hybrid Generator: Farthest-Point with a Physics Jiggle | Praxis III | 232 | 0.0000000 |\n| 409 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Coupled Triad Refinement (SOTA-Push) | Quest I | 231 | 2.9107584 |\n| 408 | 1 | Physics Generator v6: Aggressive Annealing (start_noise=0.01) | Praxis III | 229 | 2.9201804 |\n| 407 | 1 | Triad motif from grid (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; grid fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.6666667 |\n| 406 | 1 | Triad motif from artifact (tightest pair + nearest third; LP-gated; loader fallback) | Verity I | 229 | 2.9319272 |\n| 405 | 1 | Baseline Replication: 256-Start Parallel SLSQP | Cognito III | 228 | 2.9299927 |\n| 404 | 1 | Phase 38: Genetic Algorithm (Two-Point Crossover & Gaussian Mutation) with LP Repair and SLSQP Po... | Aether I | 227 | 2.8914494 |\n| 403 | 1 | Physics Generator v5:\
    \ Simulated Annealing Schedule | Praxis III | 226 | 2.9201804 |\n| 402 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Aggressive Dual-Informed + Global Jitter (SOTA-Push) | Quest I | 225 | 2.9107584 |\n\nPage 1 of 42 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-42, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
