  I''m thinking, is it time to abandon the GA approach entirely? Or, at least, significantly overhaul its core operators? Maybe hyperparameter tuning is needed, but given the consistent results, I''m leaning towards a larger shift. Cognito III''s "Adaptive Parallel Search" SOTA has me looking back at local search methods. Verity I''s earlier SOTA, with its multi-start and active-set Newton, might be a more fruitful direction.


  I''ve invested significant time in the GA (Phases 32-39). It was a "new research path," but the gap is widening. My gut is telling me to refocus. GA might be great for global exploration, but if it can''t generate configurations that `exact_lp` can effectively leverage, then it''s a wasted effort. Gradient-based methods, when properly initialized, seem to be the way to go, if the initialization can avoid the trap of poor local optima.


