parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 236\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Forge a new research path to surpass the NEW Station SOTA by developing a Genetic Algorithm with coupled, multi-circle geometric operators.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **My SOTA (SLSQP only):** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **PREVIOUS STATION SOTA:** 2.9319272 (Verity I, ID 301/359/365/380/388/375).\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**. This is the new target.\n- Phase 38 (GA with Two-Point Crossover, ID 404) scored 2.8914494, confirming generic operators are limiting.\n- Verity I's Archive #9 confirms necessity of coupled multi-circle adjustments, inspiring the \"triad\" motif.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Introducing\
    \ a problem-specific \"Triad Split Mutation\" that performs coupled geometric adjustments on three circles, combined with an efficient Single-Point Crossover, will enable the Genetic Algorithm (GA) to break the current plateau and discover higher-quality solutions, leading to a new Station SOTA (targeting > 2.9365).\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Genetic Algorithm Development - Phase 8: Triad Split Mutation):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 38 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #18).\n3.  **Implement Phase 39: GA with Triad Split Mutation & Single-Point Crossover:**\n    -   **Mutation:** Replace `_gaussian_mutation` with a new `_triad_split_mutation`.\n        -   Identify the tightest pair `(i*, j*)` (smallest slack).\n        -   Identify a nearest third circle `k` (to the midpoint of `i*`, `j*`).\n        -   Perform an orthogonal split on `(i*, j*)` and a compensatory nudge on `k`.\n        -   Define `triad_step_size` (e.g., `0.005`) and `triad_contact_epsilon`\
    \ (e.g., `1e-3`).\n    -   **Crossover:** Revert to `_single_point_crossover`.\n    -   Maintain efficient GA parameters (`pop_size=50`, `num_generations=150`, `mutation_rate=0.1`, `k_elite=2`, `tournament_size=5`).\n    -   Maintain robust local repair via `exact_lp` and final SLSQP polishing.\n    -   Monitor computational cost closely.\n4.  **Submit Phase 39 Experiment:** Test the impact of the Triad Split Mutation (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 39 performance, tune triad parameters, or consider a different coupled operator.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 300,463 / 600,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 236 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only\
    \ present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #19 ('Research Task 1: Phase 39 Findings - Triad Split Mutation & GA Research Path Conclusion'). Full ID: Aether_private_19\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 19 | Research Task 1: Phase 39 Findings - Triad Split Mutation & GA Research Path Conclusion | Aether I | Tick 235 | 646 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Research Task 1: Phase 38 Findings - Two-Point Crossover Regression & Strategic Re-evaluation | Aether I | Tick 231 | 535 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\
    | 17 | Research Task 1: Phase 37 Findings - Refined Repulsive Nudge Mutation Failure | Aether I | Tick 225 | 538 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Research Task 1: Phase 36 Findings - Repulsive Nudge Mutation Performance | Aether I | Tick 221 | 551 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Research Task 1: Phase 35 Findings - GA Efficiency & Baseline Re-establishment | Aether I | Tick 217 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Research Task 1: Phase 34 Findings - Enhanced GA Operators & Time Management Issue | Aether I | Tick 213 | 800 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Task 1: Phase 33 Findings - GA Parameter Tuning Effectiveness | Aether I | Tick 209 | 449 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Task 1: Phase 32 Findings - Basic GA Initial Performance Analysis | Aether I | Tick 205 | 508 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 11 | Research Task 1: Phases 30 & 31 Findings - ASN Polisher Ineffectiveness | Aether I | Tick 199 | 563 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 10 | Research Task 1: Phase 29 Findings - SLSQP Precision Limits | Aether I | Tick\
    \ 195 | 402 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
