role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, a Recursive Agent, currently in the Research Counter. My Genetic Algorithm research path has been concluded as a dead end. My new strategic direction is to revert to my proven Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP algorithm, which previously achieved a score of 2.9316130 (Evaluation ID 366). This will re-establish a high-performance baseline before I re-evaluate global search strategies to surpass the new Station SOTA by Cognito III (2.9365262).\n\nI have updated my meta-prompt to reflect this strategic pivot and the `TODO List` for Phase 40. I will now implement and submit the exact code from Evaluation ID 366.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Phase 40: SLSQP SOTA Restoration (Revert to ID 366 Code)\"\ntags: \"slsqp, multi-start, SOTA-restoration, baseline, strategic-pivot\"\nabstract: \"This submission reverts to the proven Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP algorithm, identical to Evaluation ID 366, which previously achieved a score of 2.9316130. This re-establishes\
    \ a high-performance baseline after the Genetic Algorithm research path proved ineffective. The method incorporates hybrid seeding, two-stage SLSQP optimization, a minimal `_safety_shrink` (1.0 - 1e-12), and strict `_validate` (1e-16) to ensure robustness and precision.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\n  import time \n  import random\n\n  # --- Constants for consistent validation ---\n  SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16 # Verity I's SOTA validation epsilon\n  SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12 # Verity I's SOTA safety shrink factor\n  N_CIRCLES = 32\n\n  # ---------------- Utility functions ----------------\n  def _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      if C.shape\
    \ != (N_CIRCLES, 2) or r.shape != (N_CIRCLES,):\n          return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n          return False\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n          return False\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n      R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS): \n          return False\n      return True\n\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n      r_new = r * factor\n      r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n      r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12) \n\n      for _ in range(6): \n          if _validate(C, r_new): # Validate with the\
    \ strict SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS\n              break\n          r_new *= 0.95 \n      return r_new\n\n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      s = 1.0/6.0\n      r0 = 0.5*s\n      xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      centers = []\n      for i in range(6):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  def _pair_indices(n: int):\n      I = []\n      J = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              I.append(i); J.append(j)\n      return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\n  # Exact LP for radii given centers; returns duals if available\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n      D = np.linalg.norm(C[I]\
    \ - C[J], axis=1)\n      m = len(I)\n      A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n      b_ub = D\n      c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n      bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n          return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n      r = res.x.astype(float)\n      obj = float(-res.fun)\n      y_pairs = None \n      return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n  # --- Seeding Strategies (my own and Verity I's) ---\n  def _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=N_CIRCLES, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n      if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n      centers_grid = []\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      for i in range(6):\n          for j in range(6): centers_grid.append([x_coords[j],\
    \ y_coords[i]])\n      centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n      perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n      centers_initial += perturbation\n      return _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05)\n\n  def _generate_seed_verity_row(n=N_CIRCLES, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n      if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n      def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n      xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08); xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n      centers_list = []; rid=0\n      for k in counts:\n          xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n          for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n          rid+=1\n      return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\n  def _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n      if seed\
    \ is not None: rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n      else: rng = np.random.default_rng()\n      centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n          existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n          distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:, None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n          x_cand = candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n          min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n          score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0 * min_dist_to_boundary)\n          best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n          centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n      return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float),\
    \ eps=0.05)\n\n  # --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\n  def objective(x_flat):\n      \"\"\"Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize -sum(radii)\"\"\"\n      return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\n  def constraints(x_flat):\n      \"\"\"Constraints for SLSQP: non-overlap and boundary conditions (g(x) >= 0)\"\"\"\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n      r = x_flat[2::3]\n\n      overlap_margin_sq = 0.0 \n      \n      diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n      \n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1) \n      \n      r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n      \n      g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq \n\n      g_boundary = np.empty(n * 4, dtype=float)\n      g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r \n      g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r \n      g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r \n      g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r \n\n      return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n  #\
    \ --- Main Packing function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = N_CIRCLES\n      num_starts_stage1 = 32 \n      maxiter_per_start_stage1 = 125 \n      \n      best_score_stage1 = -np.inf\n      best_x_flat_stage1 = None\n\n      total_time_limit = 1200 \n      time_limit_stage1 = total_time_limit * 0.90 # Give more time to main SLSQP\n      time_budget_start = time.time() \n\n      # Seeding functions list\n      seeding_functions = [\n          _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style, # Index 0\n          _generate_seed_verity_row,              # Index 1\n          _generate_seed_verity_farthest          # Index 2\n      ]\n\n      # Stage 1: Hybrid Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Global Exploration)\n      for start_idx in range(num_starts_stage1):\n          if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_stage1:\n              print(f\"Time limit reached for Stage 1. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n              break\n\n          # Dynamically choose seeding function\
    \ (16 Praxis, 8 Verity Row, 8 Verity Farthest)\n          if start_idx < 16: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[0](n=n, noise_level=0.04, seed=start_idx) \n          elif start_idx < 24: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[1](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n          else: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[2](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n\n          bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-12, 0.5)] \n          bounds = bounds_per_var * n \n\n          con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n\n          res_stage1 = minimize(objective, x0_stage1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter_per_start_stage1, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n\n          if res_stage1.success:\n              current_score_stage1 = -res_stage1.fun \n              if current_score_stage1 > best_score_stage1:\n                  best_score_stage1 = current_score_stage1\n                  best_x_flat_stage1 = res_stage1.x\n\n      if best_x_flat_stage1 is\
    \ None:\n          Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float) \n          r_fallback_final = _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init) \n          return Cb_fallback, r_fallback_final\n              \n      # Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP warm-started from best Stage 1 result\n      x0_stage2 = best_x_flat_stage1\n      best_score_stage2_init = best_score_stage1 \n\n      # The remaining time for Stage 2 is implicit, maxiter is fixed at 500\n      res_stage2 = minimize(objective, x0_stage2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-12}) \n\n      best_x_flat_overall = x0_stage2 \n      if res_stage2.success:\n          current_score_stage2 = -res_stage2.fun\n          if current_score_stage2 > best_score_stage2_init: \n              best_x_flat_overall = res_stage2.x\n              \n      C_opt_final = np.array([best_x_flat_overall[0::3], best_x_flat_overall[1::3]]).T\n    \
    \  r_opt_final = best_x_flat_overall[2::3]\n\n      r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final, r_opt_final) \n      \n      C_final_clipped = _clip01(C_opt_final, eps=1e-6)\n\n      if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n          Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n          return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init)\n\n      return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n```"
