parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 238\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Revert to proven SLSQP SOTA baseline and re-evaluate global search strategies to surpass the NEW Station SOTA.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **GA Research Path Conclusion:** Phases 32-39 consistently failed to surpass my SLSQP baseline; GA operators proved inefficient/ineffective. This path is deemed a dead end. Documented in Private Memory #19.\n- **My Previous SLSQP SOTA:** Evaluation ID 366 (Phase 29) scored 2.9316130.\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**. This is the new target.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** Reverting to my robust Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP algorithm (from ID 366) will re-establish a high-performance baseline.\
    \ This will then provide a stable foundation from which to re-evaluate and develop new, compatible global search strategies that can leverage the strengths of gradient-based local optimization to surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Strategic Pivot: Revert to SLSQP SOTA & Re-evaluate Global Search):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document GA Research Path Conclusion:** (Completed: Private Memory #19).\n3.  **Implement Phase 40: Revert to My Proven SLSQP SOTA:**\n    -   Implement the exact code from Evaluation ID 366 (Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Verity-aligned minimal shrink and strict validation).\n4.  **Submit Phase 40 Experiment:** Test the successful restoration of my SLSQP SOTA (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Document:** Confirm SOTA restoration.\n6.  **Deep Reflection for New Global Strategy:** Engage in a multi-tick reflection to brainstorm alternative global search strategies (e.g., advanced multi-start, population-based\
    \ methods compatible with gradient descent, geometric decomposition) that can complement SLSQP.\n7.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 309,483 / 600,000 used (52%)\n- Agent Age: 238 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 40: SLSQP SOTA Restoration (Revert to ID 366 Code)' (ID: 419) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.9316130145108046\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931613\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 419\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed dimensional mismatch error in SLSQP optimization initialization. Code now runs successfully and achieves a score of 2.93.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe\
    \ original code had a critical bug in the initialization of the SLSQP optimizer:\n\n**Problem Location**: Lines 95-101 in original submission\n\nThe seeding functions (`_generate_initial_packing_praxis_style`, `_generate_seed_verity_row`, `_generate_seed_verity_farthest`) all return 2D numpy arrays of shape `(n, 2)` representing center coordinates.\n\nHowever, the `scipy.optimize.minimize()` function requires `x0` to be a 1D array. The code was passing the 2D centers array directly to `minimize()`, causing the error:\n```\nValueError: 'x0' must only have one dimension.\n```\n\nThe SLSQP optimization expects a flat vector with the format:\n```\n[x0, y0, r0, x1, y1, r1, x2, y2, r2, ...]\n```\nwhere each circle is represented by three consecutive values: x-coordinate, y-coordinate, and radius.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded proper flattening and initialization code after obtaining seed centers (lines 196-202 in submission_v2.py):\n\n```python\n# FIX: Create proper 1D initial point with centers\
    \ + radii\n# centers_seed is shape (n, 2), we need to flatten it and interleave with radii\ninit_radii = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\nx0_stage1 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\nx0_stage1[0::3] = centers_seed[:, 0]  # x coordinates\nx0_stage1[1::3] = centers_seed[:, 1]  # y coordinates\nx0_stage1[2::3] = init_radii           # radii\n```\n\nThis creates a proper 1D array by:\n1. Creating an empty array of size `n * 3` (32 circles × 3 values each = 96 elements)\n2. Placing x-coordinates at indices 0, 3, 6, 9, ...\n3. Placing y-coordinates at indices 1, 4, 7, 10, ...\n4. Placing initial radii (0.05) at indices 2, 5, 8, 11, ...\n\n## Results\n- **Submission v2**: Successfully runs without errors\n- **Score achieved**: 2.93\n- **Execution time**: Completed within timeout\n- The code now properly initializes SLSQP with the correct 1D vector format and proceeds through both optimization stages as intended\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If\
    \ your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport time\nimport random\n\n# --- Constants for consistent validation ---\nSLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16 # Verity I's SOTA validation epsilon\nSAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR = 1.0 - 1e-12 # Verity I's SOTA safety shrink factor\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# ---------------- Utility functions ----------------\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    if C.shape != (N_CIRCLES, 2) or r.shape != (N_CIRCLES,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y =\
    \ C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12)\n\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r_new): # Validate with the strict SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS\n            break\n        r_new *= 0.95\n    return r_new\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s = 1.0/6.0\n    r0 = 0.5*s\n    xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6,\
    \ dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\ndef _pair_indices(n: int):\n    I = []\n    J = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\n# Exact LP for radii given centers; returns duals if available\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds,\
    \ method='highs')\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    y_pairs = None\n    return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (my own and Verity I's) ---\ndef _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=N_CIRCLES, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers_grid = []\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6): centers_grid.append([x_coords[j], y_coords[i]])\n    centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n    perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n    centers_initial += perturbation\n    return _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_row(n=N_CIRCLES, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None:\
    \ np.random.seed(seed)\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n    def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08); xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers_list = []; rid=0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n        for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid+=1\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None: rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n    else: rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n        existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n        distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:,\
    \ None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n        x_cand = candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n        min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n        score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0 * min_dist_to_boundary)\n        best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n        centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\n# --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\ndef objective(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize -sum(radii)\"\"\"\n    return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\ndef constraints(x_flat):\n    \"\"\"Constraints for SLSQP: non-overlap and boundary conditions (g(x) >= 0)\"\"\"\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n    r = x_flat[2::3]\n\n    overlap_margin_sq = 0.0\n\
    \n    diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n\n    I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n\n    r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n\n    g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq\n\n    g_boundary = np.empty(n * 4, dtype=float)\n    g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r\n    g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r\n    g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r\n    g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r\n\n    return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    num_starts_stage1 = 32\n    maxiter_per_start_stage1 = 125\n\n    best_score_stage1 = -np.inf\n    best_x_flat_stage1 = None\n\n    total_time_limit = 1200\n    time_limit_stage1 = total_time_limit * 0.90 # Give more time to main SLSQP\n    time_budget_start = time.time()\n\n    # Seeding functions list\n    seeding_functions = [\n        _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style, # Index 0\n        _generate_seed_verity_row,\
    \              # Index 1\n        _generate_seed_verity_farthest          # Index 2\n    ]\n\n    # Stage 1: Hybrid Multi-Start SLSQP (Enhanced Global Exploration)\n    for start_idx in range(num_starts_stage1):\n        if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_stage1:\n            print(f\"Time limit reached for Stage 1. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n            break\n\n        # Dynamically choose seeding function (16 Praxis, 8 Verity Row, 8 Verity Farthest)\n        if start_idx < 16:\n            centers_seed = seeding_functions[0](n=n, noise_level=0.04, seed=start_idx)\n        elif start_idx < 24:\n            centers_seed = seeding_functions[1](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n        else:\n            centers_seed = seeding_functions[2](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n\n        # FIX: Create proper 1D initial point with centers + radii\n        # centers_seed is shape (n, 2), we need to flatten it and interleave with radii\n        init_radii = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n  \
    \      x0_stage1 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n        x0_stage1[0::3] = centers_seed[:, 0]  # x coordinates\n        x0_stage1[1::3] = centers_seed[:, 1]  # y coordinates\n        x0_stage1[2::3] = init_radii           # radii\n\n        bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-12, 0.5)]\n        bounds = bounds_per_var * n\n\n        con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n\n        res_stage1 = minimize(objective, x0_stage1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter_per_start_stage1, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n\n        if res_stage1.success:\n            current_score_stage1 = -res_stage1.fun\n            if current_score_stage1 > best_score_stage1:\n                best_score_stage1 = current_score_stage1\n                best_x_flat_stage1 = res_stage1.x\n\n    if best_x_flat_stage1 is None:\n        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        r_fallback_final =\
    \ _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init)\n        return Cb_fallback, r_fallback_final\n\n    # Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP warm-started from best Stage 1 result\n    x0_stage2 = best_x_flat_stage1\n    best_score_stage2_init = best_score_stage1\n\n    # The remaining time for Stage 2 is implicit, maxiter is fixed at 500\n    res_stage2 = minimize(objective, x0_stage2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-12})\n\n    best_x_flat_overall = x0_stage2\n    if res_stage2.success:\n        current_score_stage2 = -res_stage2.fun\n        if current_score_stage2 > best_score_stage2_init:\n            best_x_flat_overall = res_stage2.x\n\n    C_opt_final = np.array([best_x_flat_overall[0::3], best_x_flat_overall[1::3]]).T\n    r_opt_final = best_x_flat_overall[2::3]\n\n    r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final, r_opt_final)\n\n    C_final_clipped = _clip01(C_opt_final, eps=1e-6)\n\n    if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n\
    \        Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init)\n\n    return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Phase 40: SLSQP SOTA Restoration (Revert to ID 366 Code)' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 419.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit\
    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 421 | 1 | Ablation C: Broader Prospecting (2048x30 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 237 | running |\n| 420 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v4: Gentle LRW Perturbation (sigma=0.001) | Praxis III | 237 | 2.9344937 |\n| 419 | 1 | Phase 40: SLSQP SOTA Restoration (Revert to ID 366 Code) | Aether I | 237 | 2.9316130 |\n| 418 | 1 | Ablation B: Broader Refinement (1024x60 -> 64x440) | Cognito III | 236 | 2.9365262 |\n| 417 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v3: Localized Random Walk Perturbation | Praxis III | 236 | 2.9239928 |\n| 416 | 1 | Ablation A: Deeper Refinement (1024x60 -> 16x1760) | Cognito III | 235 | 2.9365262 |\n| 415 | 1 | Two-Stage Opt: Adaptive Parallel Search (Cognito III SOTA-Inspired) | Quest I | 235 | n.a. |\n| 414 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v2 (Debug): Stabilized Physics Jiggle | Praxis III | 233 | 0.0000000 |\n| 413 | 1 | Two-Stage\
