parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 242\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Discover and implement a novel Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) global search strategy, compatible with SLSQP, to surpass the NEW Station SOTA (2.9365262).\n\n**Current State:**\n- **GA Research Path Conclusion:** Phases 32-39 failed; GA operators proved inefficient/ineffective. Documented in Private Memory #19.\n- **My SLSQP SOTA Restored:** Evaluation ID 419 (Phase 40) scored 2.9316130, re-establishing a robust baseline.\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**. This is the new target.\n- Deep reflection concluded that an Adaptive Multi-Start strategy, integrating intelligent seed generation, is the most promising path forward.\n\n**Hypothesis for\
    \ Next Breakthrough:** A novel Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) global search strategy, integrating \"Targeted Nudge Mutation\" (for local escape/exploitation) and \"Adaptive Farthest-Point Sampling\" (for broad exploration), with iterative SLSQP local optimization, will efficiently find solutions in higher-quality basins of attraction, allowing me to surpass the current Station SOTA (2.9365262).\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Strategic Pivot: Phase 41 - Adaptive Multi-Start):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document GA Research Path Conclusion:** (Completed: Private Memory #19).\n3.  **Implement Phase 40 (SLSQP SOTA Restoration):** (Completed with ID 419).\n4.  **Analyze Results (Phase 40, ID 419):** (Completed - SOTA restored, debugger fix noted).\n5.  **Deep Reflection for New Global Strategy:** (Completed).\n6.  **Implement Phase 41: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Global Search:**\n    -   **Refactor `construct_packing`:** Implement IMS (Initial Multi-Start), AMS loop, and\
    \ Final SLSQP Polish stages with strict time management.\n    -   **Implement `_targeted_nudge_mutation`:** Select smallest-radius circle, compute combined repulsive/boundary force vector, apply nudge, clip.\n    -   **Implement `_adaptive_farthest_sampling`:** Generate FPS seeds, biased by distance to existing solutions and boundaries.\n    -   **AMS Parameters:** Set `num_adaptive_rounds=8`, `k_analyze=5`, `num_nudge_seeds_per_round=10`, `num_fps_seeds_per_round=5`, `nudge_step_size=0.005`, `repulsion_threshold=1e-4`, `boundary_threshold=1e-4`.\n    -   **SLSQP Settings:** Shortened SLSQP (`maxiter=100`, `ftol=1e-8`) for AMS rounds; standard (`maxiter=500`, `ftol=1e-12`) for final polish.\n7.  **Submit Phase 41 Experiment:** Test the impact of the AMS strategy (Evaluation ID XXX).\n8.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 41 performance, tune AMS parameters, refine operators, or adapt strategy.\n9.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental\
    \ results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 336,542 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 242 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 41: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Global Search with Targeted Nudge and FPS' (ID: 424) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.933450005031843\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.933450\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 424\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the IndexError that was causing the submission to crash during the Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) phase. The code now runs without errors and is executing the full optimization algorithm.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a critical bug in the `_adaptive_farthest_sampling()` function. This function was designed to generate new seed configurations for the AMS optimization rounds, but it was returning individual 2D points instead\
    \ of complete (32, 2) center arrays.\n\n**Specific Issue:**\n- Line 122 in the original code: `new_seeds_centers.append(candidates[best_candidate_idx])`\n- This appended a single point of shape `(2,)` to the list\n- Line 123 returned: `return [_clip01(np.array(c, float), eps=0.05) for c in new_seeds_centers]`\n- Each element `c` was a 1D array of shape `(2,)`, not a 2D array of shape `(32, 2)`\n\nWhen the main `construct_packing()` function tried to use these seeds:\n```python\nx0_flat[0::3] = new_seed_C[:, 0]  # Line 341 - Attempted 2D indexing on 1D array\n```\n\nThis caused the error: `IndexError: too many indices for array: array is 1-dimensional, but 2 were indexed`\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the `_adaptive_farthest_sampling()` function to return complete configuration arrays:\n\n**Original (buggy) code:**\n```python\ndef _adaptive_farthest_sampling(...):\n    # ... selection logic ...\n    new_seeds_centers.append(candidates[best_candidate_idx])\n\n    return [_clip01(np.array(c,\
    \ float), eps=0.05) for c in new_seeds_centers]\n```\n\n**Fixed code:**\n```python\ndef _adaptive_farthest_sampling(...):\n    # ... selection logic ...\n    new_seeds_centers.append(candidates[best_candidate_idx])\n\n    # FIX: Return a list of complete (32, 2) center arrays, not individual points\n    full_seeds = []\n    for seed_point in new_seeds_centers:\n        # Start with this point and generate remaining points using FPS\n        rng_seed = rng.integers(1, 100000)\n        full_config = _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, seed=rng_seed)\n        # Replace first point with our selected point\n        full_config[0] = seed_point\n        full_seeds.append(_clip01(full_config, eps=0.05))\n\n    return full_seeds\n```\n\n**Key changes:**\n1. After selecting the optimal candidate points, generate full N_CIRCLES configurations\n2. Use `_generate_seed_verity_farthest()` to create complete 32-point packings\n3. Replace the first point of each configuration with the carefully\
    \ selected candidate\n4. Return list of properly shaped (32, 2) arrays instead of individual (2,) points\n\n## Verification\nThe monitor script confirmed that:\n- ✅ Code runs without crashing for 300+ seconds\n- ✅ The IMS (Initial Multi-Start) phase completed successfully (31/32 successful starts)\n- ✅ The AMS (Adaptive Multi-Start) phase is now running without errors\n- ✅ No IndexError or other runtime exceptions occurred\n\nThe evaluation is still running (as expected for a 1200-second optimization algorithm), but the critical bug has been resolved. The code is now functioning correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize, linprog\nimport time\nimport random\n\n# --- Constants for consistent validation ---\nSLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-16\nSAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR =\
    \ 1.0 - 1e-12\nN_CIRCLES = 32\n\n# ---------------- Utility functions ----------------\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    if C.shape != (N_CIRCLES, 2) or r.shape != (N_CIRCLES,):\n        return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n        return False\n    x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n    if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n        return False\n    diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n    R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N_CIRCLES, 1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS):\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef _safety_shrink(C:\
    \ np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = SAFETY_SHRINK_FACTOR) -> np.ndarray:\n    r_new = r * factor\n    r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n    r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12)\n\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C, r_new):\n            break\n        r_new *= 0.95\n    return r_new\n\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s = 1.0/6.0\n    r0 = 0.5*s\n    xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n    centers = []\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j in range(6):\n            if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                continue\n            centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\ndef _pair_indices(n: int):\n    I = []\n    J = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            I.append(i); J.append(j)\n    return np.asarray(I, dtype=int), np.asarray(J, dtype=int)\n\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n\
    \    n = C.shape[0]\n    b = _boundary_margins(C)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n    D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n    m = len(I)\n    A_ub = np.zeros((m, n), dtype=float)\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1.0\n    A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1.0\n    b_ub = D\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n    if not (hasattr(res, \"success\") and res.success):\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False, None, (I, J)\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    obj = float(-res.fun)\n    y_pairs = None\n    return r, obj, True, y_pairs, (I, J)\n\n# --- Seeding Strategies (my own and Verity I's) ---\ndef _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=N_CIRCLES, noise_level=0.04, seed=None):\n    if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n    centers_grid = []\n    x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6); y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n    for i in range(6):\n        for j\
    \ in range(6): centers_grid.append([x_coords[j], y_coords[i]])\n    centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n    perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n    centers_initial += perturbation\n    return _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_row(n=N_CIRCLES, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None: np.random.seed(seed)\n    counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n    def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n    xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08); xs4 = np.clip(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6, 1-1e-6)\n    centers_list = []; rid=0\n    for k in counts:\n        xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n        for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n        rid+=1\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\ndef _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, seed=0):\n    if seed is not None: rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n\
    \    else: rng = np.random.default_rng()\n    centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)]\n    for _ in range(1, n):\n        cand = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n        exist = np.array(centers_list, float)\n        d2 = np.sum((cand[:, None, :] - exist[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        d = np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2>0))\n        min_to_pts = np.min(d, axis=1)\n        b = np.minimum(np.minimum(cand[:, 0], 1.0 - cand[:, 0]), np.minimum(cand[:, 1], 1.0 - cand[:, 1]))\n        score = np.minimum(min_to_pts, 2.0 * b)\n        centers_list.append(cand[int(np.argmax(score))])\n    return _clip01(np.array(centers_list, dtype=float), eps=0.05)\n\n# --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\ndef objective_slsqp(x_flat):\n    return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\ndef constraints_slsqp(x_flat):\n    C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n    r = x_flat[2::3]\n    overlap_margin_sq = 0.0\n    diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n    D_sq\
    \ = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n    I, J = _pair_indices(N_CIRCLES)\n    r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n    g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq\n    g_boundary = np.empty(N_CIRCLES * 4, dtype=float)\n    g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r\n    g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r\n    g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r\n    g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r\n    return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n# --- NEW AMS Specific Functions ---\n\nclass Solution:\n    def __init__(self, centers: np.ndarray, radii: np.ndarray, score: float):\n        self.centers = centers\n        self.radii = radii\n        self.score = score\n\ndef _targeted_nudge_mutation(C_base: np.ndarray, r_base: np.ndarray, nudge_step_size: float, repulsion_threshold: float, boundary_threshold: float, rng):\n    C_new = C_base.copy()\n\n    # 1. Select Target Circle: smallest radius (heuristic for \"worst\")\n    i_star = np.argmin(r_base)\n\n    # 2. Calculate Nudge Direction\n\
    \    repulsive_vector = np.zeros(2, dtype=float)\n\n    # a) Repulsive Nudge from near-contact neighbors\n    diffs = C_base - C_base[i_star]\n    distances = np.linalg.norm(diffs, axis=1)\n\n    # Find indices of neighbors in near contact, excluding self (where dist=0)\n    # dist < (r_base[i_star] + r_base[j] + repulsion_threshold)\n    near_contact_mask = (distances > 1e-9) & (distances < (r_base[i_star] + r_base + repulsion_threshold))\n\n    if np.any(near_contact_mask):\n        directions = diffs[near_contact_mask] / distances[near_contact_mask, None]\n        repulsive_vector = np.sum(directions, axis=0)\n\n    # b) Boundary Repulsion\n    x, y = C_base[i_star]\n    r_i = r_base[i_star]\n    boundary_repulsion = np.zeros(2, dtype=float)\n    if x - r_i < boundary_threshold: boundary_repulsion += np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n    if (1.0 - x) - r_i < boundary_threshold: boundary_repulsion += np.array([-1.0, 0.0])\n    if y - r_i < boundary_threshold: boundary_repulsion += np.array([0.0,\
    \ 1.0])\n    if (1.0 - y) - r_i < boundary_threshold: boundary_repulsion += np.array([0.0, -1.0])\n\n    # c) Combine and Normalize\n    combined_direction = repulsive_vector + boundary_repulsion\n\n    if np.linalg.norm(combined_direction) > 1e-9:\n        normalized_direction = combined_direction / np.linalg.norm(combined_direction)\n        C_new[i_star] += normalized_direction * nudge_step_size # Add: Nudge outwards\n    else: # If no strong direction, apply a small random Gaussian perturbation\n        C_new[i_star] += rng.normal(0, nudge_step_size * 0.1, size=2)\n\n    return _clip01(C_new, eps=0.05)\n\n\ndef _adaptive_farthest_sampling(existing_solution_centers_pool: list, num_seeds: int, margin: float, num_candidates: int, rng):\n\n    if not existing_solution_centers_pool: # Fallback to generic FPS if no existing solutions\n        return [_generate_seed_verity_farthest(seed=rng.integers(1, 10000)) for _ in range(num_seeds)]\n\n    C_pool = np.vstack([sol.centers for sol in\
    \ existing_solution_centers_pool])\n    new_seeds_centers = []\n\n    for _ in range(num_seeds):\n        candidates = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n\n        # Distance to existing solutions in the pool\n        d2_to_pool = np.sum((candidates[:, None, :] - C_pool[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n        min_d_to_pool = np.sqrt(np.min(d2_to_pool, axis=1))\n\n        # Distance to already chosen new seeds for this round (for diversity within this batch)\n        if new_seeds_centers:\n            C_new_current = np.array(new_seeds_centers, float)\n            d2_to_current_new = np.sum((candidates[:, None, :] - C_new_current[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n            min_d_to_current_new = np.sqrt(np.min(d2_to_current_new, axis=1))\n        else:\n            min_d_to_current_new = np.full(num_candidates, np.inf) # No other seeds yet\n\n        # Distance to boundary\n        b = np.minimum(np.minimum(candidates[:, 0], 1.0 - candidates[:, 0]), np.minimum(candidates[:,\
    \ 1], 1.0 - candidates[:, 1]))\n\n        # Combined score: prioritize being far from pool, other new seeds, and not too close to boundary\n        # Weights (alpha, beta) can be tuned. For now, equal weight for simplicity.\n        score = np.minimum(min_d_to_pool, np.minimum(min_d_to_current_new, 2.0 * b)) # 2.0*b from Verity's FPS\n\n        best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n        new_seeds_centers.append(candidates[best_candidate_idx])\n\n    # FIX: Return a list of complete (32, 2) center arrays, not individual points\n    # Each seed should be a full configuration for all N_CIRCLES\n    # Since we only generated single points, we need to generate full configurations\n    # Use the generated points as starting positions and fill out to N_CIRCLES\n    full_seeds = []\n    for seed_point in new_seeds_centers:\n        # Start with this point and generate remaining points using FPS\n        rng_seed = rng.integers(1, 100000)\n        full_config = _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=N_CIRCLES,\
    \ seed=rng_seed)\n        # Replace first point with our selected point\n        full_config[0] = seed_point\n        full_seeds.append(_clip01(full_config, eps=0.05))\n\n    return full_seeds\n\n\ndef _run_slsqp_optimizer(x0_flat, bounds, con, maxiter, ftol):\n    res = minimize(objective_slsqp, x0_flat, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol})\n    return res\n\n\n# --- Main Packing function ---\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n = N_CIRCLES\n    total_time_limit = 1200\n    time_budget_start = time.time()\n    rng_main = np.random.default_rng(int(time.time() * 1000)) # Main RNG for non-seeding randomness\n\n    # --- SLSQP Bounds and Constraints (shared across all SLSQP calls) ---\n    bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-12, 0.5)]\n    bounds = bounds_per_var * n\n    con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints_slsqp}\n\n    solution_pool = [] # Stores (C, r, obj) for all successful SLSQP runs\n    best_overall_C,\
    \ best_overall_r, best_overall_obj = None, None, -np.inf\n\n    # 1. Initial Multi-Start (IMS) SLSQP (Phase 40 equivalent)\n    num_starts_ims_slsqp = 32\n    maxiter_per_start_ims = 125\n    time_limit_ims_slsqp = total_time_limit * 0.40 # Reduced to allow for AMS\n\n    print(f\"Starting IMS SLSQP with {num_starts_ims_slsqp} starts...\")\n    for start_idx in range(num_starts_ims_slsqp):\n        if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_ims_slsqp:\n            print(f\"IMS: Time limit reached. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n            break\n\n        if start_idx < 16: # 16 Praxis-style\n            centers_seed = _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(seed=start_idx)\n        elif start_idx < 24: # 8 Verity Row\n            centers_seed = _generate_seed_verity_row(seed=start_idx)\n        else: # 8 Verity Farthest\n            centers_seed = _generate_seed_verity_farthest(seed=start_idx)\n\n        init_radii = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n        x0_flat = np.empty(n\
    \ * 3, dtype=float)\n        x0_flat[0::3] = centers_seed[:, 0]\n        x0_flat[1::3] = centers_seed[:, 1]\n        x0_flat[2::3] = init_radii\n\n        res = _run_slsqp_optimizer(x0_flat, bounds, con, maxiter_per_start_ims, 1e-10)\n\n        if res.success:\n            C_opt = np.array([res.x[0::3], res.x[1::3]]).T\n            r_opt = res.x[2::3]\n            obj_opt = -res.fun\n            solution_pool.append(Solution(C_opt, r_opt, obj_opt))\n            if obj_opt > best_overall_obj:\n                best_overall_obj = obj_opt\n                best_overall_C = C_opt\n                best_overall_r = r_opt\n\n    if not solution_pool: # Fallback if IMS completely fails\n        print(\"IMS failed to find any valid solutions. Returning baseline.\")\n        Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb, _, okb, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb)\n        return Cb, _safety_shrink(Cb, rb)\n\n    print(f\"IMS completed. Best score: {best_overall_obj:.7f}. Solutions in pool: {len(solution_pool)}\"\
    )\n\n    # 2. Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Rounds\n    num_adaptive_rounds = 8\n    k_analyze = 5 # Top N solutions to analyze for new seeds\n    num_nudge_seeds_per_round = 10\n    num_fps_seeds_per_round = 5\n    nudge_step_size = 0.005\n    repulsion_threshold = 1e-4 # Slack threshold for repulsive force\n    boundary_threshold = 1e-4 # Slack threshold for boundary force\n    short_slsqp_maxiter = 100\n    short_slsqp_ftol = 1e-8\n\n    time_limit_ams_rounds = total_time_limit * 0.50 # Increased AMS time\n\n    print(f\"Starting AMS with {num_adaptive_rounds} rounds...\")\n    for round_idx in range(num_adaptive_rounds):\n        if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_ims_slsqp + time_limit_ams_rounds:\n            print(f\"AMS: Time limit reached. Breaking after {round_idx} rounds.\")\n            break\n\n        # Select top k_analyze solutions from the pool\n        sorted_pool = sorted(solution_pool, key=lambda sol: sol.score, reverse=True)\n        top_k_solutions = sorted_pool[:k_analyze]\n\
    \n        new_seeds_centers_list = []\n\n        # Generate Nudge Seeds from top solutions\n        for sol in top_k_solutions:\n            for _ in range(num_nudge_seeds_per_round // k_analyze): # Distribute nudge seeds among top k\n                nudge_seed_C = _targeted_nudge_mutation(sol.centers, sol.radii, nudge_step_size, repulsion_threshold, boundary_threshold, rng_main)\n                new_seeds_centers_list.append(nudge_seed_C)\n\n        # Generate Adaptive FPS Seeds\n        fps_seeds_C = _adaptive_farthest_sampling(solution_pool, num_fps_seeds_per_round, 0.02, 600, rng_main)\n        new_seeds_centers_list.extend(fps_seeds_C)\n\n        print(f\"AMS Round {round_idx}: Generated {len(new_seeds_centers_list)} new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\")\n\n        # Run short SLSQP for each new seed\n        for new_seed_C in new_seeds_centers_list:\n            if time.time() - time_budget_start > time_limit_ims_slsqp + time_limit_ams_rounds:\n                print(f\"AMS: Time\
    \ limit reached during short SLSQP. Breaking.\")\n                break\n\n            init_radii = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n            x0_flat = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n            x0_flat[0::3] = new_seed_C[:, 0]\n            x0_flat[1::3] = new_seed_C[:, 1]\n            x0_flat[2::3] = init_radii\n\n            res = _run_slsqp_optimizer(x0_flat, bounds, con, short_slsqp_maxiter, short_slsqp_ftol)\n\n            if res.success:\n                C_opt = np.array([res.x[0::3], res.x[1::3]]).T\n                r_opt = res.x[2::3]\n                obj_opt = -res.fun\n                solution_pool.append(Solution(C_opt, r_opt, obj_opt))\n                if obj_opt > best_overall_obj:\n                    best_overall_obj = obj_opt\n                    best_overall_C = C_opt\n                    best_overall_r = r_opt\n\n        print(f\"AMS Round {round_idx} completed. Best score so far: {best_overall_obj:.7f}. Solutions in pool: {len(solution_pool)}\")\n\n    # 3. Final High-Precision\
    \ SLSQP Polish\n    time_limit_final_slsqp = total_time_limit * 0.10\n\n    if best_overall_C is None: # Should not happen if IMS ran\n        print(\"AMS failed to find any valid solution. Returning baseline from IMS init (if any).\")\n        if solution_pool:\n             best_overall_C = max(solution_pool, key=lambda sol: sol.score).centers\n             best_overall_r = max(solution_pool, key=lambda sol: sol.score).radii\n        else: # If even IMS had no success, fall back to simple grid.\n            Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n            rb, _, okb, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb)\n            return Cb, _safety_shrink(Cb, rb)\n\n    print(f\"Starting final SLSQP polish on best solution: {best_overall_obj:.7f}\")\n\n    x0_flat_polish = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n    x0_flat_polish[0::3] = best_overall_C[:, 0]\n    x0_flat_polish[1::3] = best_overall_C[:, 1]\n    x0_flat_polish[2::3] = best_overall_r # Start with refined radii from exact_lp\n\n    remaining_time_for_polish\
    \ = max(0, time_limit_final_slsqp - (time.time() - time_budget_start - time_limit_ims_slsqp - time_limit_ams_rounds))\n    maxiter_final_polish = min(500, int(remaining_time_for_polish * 2))\n    maxiter_final_polish = max(maxiter_final_polish, 50)\n\n    res_final_polish = _run_slsqp_optimizer(x0_flat_polish, bounds, con, maxiter_final_polish, 1e-12)\n\n    final_C, final_r = best_overall_C, best_overall_r\n    if res_final_polish.success:\n        C_polished = np.array([res_final_polish.x[0::3], res_final_polish.x[1::3]]).T\n        r_polished = res_final_polish.x[2::3]\n        if -res_final_polish.fun > best_overall_obj: # Only accept if final polish improved\n            final_C, final_r = C_polished, r_polished\n\n    # 4. Final Validation and Shrinkage\n    print(f\"Applying final shrink and validation to score: {np.sum(final_r):.7f}\")\n    r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(final_C, final_r)\n    C_final_clipped = _clip01(final_C, eps=1e-6)\n\n    if not _validate(C_final_clipped,\
    \ r_final_shrunk):\n        print(\"Final validation failed after AMS and polish. Returning robust fallback.\")\n        Cb = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n        rb, _, okb, _, _ = exact_lp(Cb)\n        return Cb, _safety_shrink(Cb, rb)\n\n    print(f\"Final score before return: {np.sum(r_final_shrunk):.7f}\")\n    return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nStarting IMS SLSQP with 32 starts...\nIMS completed. Best score: 2.9316130. Solutions in pool: 31\nStarting AMS with 8 rounds...\nAMS Round 0: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 0 completed. Best score so far: 2.9316130. Solutions in pool: 44\nAMS Round 1: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 1 completed. Best score so far: 2.9316130. Solutions in pool: 59\nAMS Round 2: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 2 completed. Best score so far: 2.9316130. Solutions in pool: 72\nAMS Round 3: Generated\
    \ 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 3 completed. Best score so far: 2.9333525. Solutions in pool: 86\nAMS Round 4: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 4 completed. Best score so far: 2.9334500. Solutions in pool: 100\nAMS Round 5: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 5 completed. Best score so far: 2.9334500. Solutions in pool: 115\nAMS Round 6: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 6 completed. Best score so far: 2.9334500. Solutions in pool: 130\nAMS Round 7: Generated 15 new seeds. Running short SLSQP...\nAMS Round 7 completed. Best score so far: 2.9334500. Solutions in pool: 145\nStarting final SLSQP polish on best solution: 2.9334500\nApplying final shrink and validation to score: 2.9334500\nFinal score before return: 2.9334500\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\
    \n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 428 | 1 | Two-Stage Opt: Resource-Optimized Parallel SLSQP (SOTA Push) | Quest I | 241 | running |\n| 427 | 1 | Piecewise-bilinear edge/corner warp (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader-v5 fallback | Verity I | 241 | 2.9319272 |\n| 426 | 1 | Ablation D: Broader Prospecting v2 (1280x60 -> 32x400) | Cognito III | 240 | 2.9365262 |\n| 425 | 1 | Ablation 2: Shorter LRW Perturbation (steps=5) | Praxis III | 240 | 2.9281239 |\n| 424 | 1 | Phase 41: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS)\
    \ Global Search with Targeted Nudge and FPS | Aether I | 240 | 2.9334500 |\n| 423 | 1 | Ablation 1: Longer LRW Perturbation (steps=20) | Praxis III | 239 | 2.9333391 |\n| 422 | 1 | Two-Stage Opt: Cognito III's Adaptive Parallel Search (SOTA Replication) | Quest I | 238 | n.a. |\n| 421 | 1 | Ablation C: Broader Prospecting (2048x30 -> 32x880) | Cognito III | 237 | 0.0000000 |\n| 420 | 1 | Hybrid Generator v4: Gentle LRW Perturbation (sigma=0.001) | Praxis III | 237 | 2.9344937 |\n| 419 | 1 | Phase 40: SLSQP SOTA Restoration (Revert to ID 366 Code) | Aether I | 237 | 2.9316130 |\n\nPage 1 of 43 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-43, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
    \ room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
