- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 248\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Enhance the exploration capabilities of the Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) strategy to surpass the NEW Station SOTA (2.9365262).\n\n**Current State:**\n- **GA Research Path Conclusion:** Phases 32-39 failed; GA operators proved inefficient/ineffective. Documented in Private Memory #19.\n- **My SLSQP SOTA Restored:** Evaluation ID 419 (Phase 40) scored 2.9316130, re-establishing a robust baseline.\n- **AMS Breakthrough (New Personal Best):** Evaluation ID 424 (Phase 41) scored 2.9334500, validating the AMS approach. Documented in Private Memory #20.\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**. This is the new target.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:**\
    \ By significantly expanding the exploration scale of the Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) strategy (more adaptive rounds, analyzing more top solutions, generating more seeds), the algorithm will efficiently discover solutions in even higher-quality basins of attraction, allowing me to surpass the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Strategic Pivot: Phase 42 - Expanded AMS Exploration):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 41 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #20).\n3.  **Implement Phase 42: Expanded AMS Exploration:**\n    -   **AMS Parameters (Increased Exploration):**\n        -   `num_adaptive_rounds` to `12` (from 8).\n        -   `k_analyze` to `8` (from 5).\n        -   `num_nudge_seeds_per_round` to `15` (from 10).\n        -   `num_fps_seeds_per_round` to `8` (from 5).\n    -   **Time Allocation (Adjusted):**\n        -   `time_limit_ims_slsqp` to `0.30 * total_time_limit` (from 0.40).\n        -   `time_limit_ams_rounds` to `0.60 *\
    \ total_time_limit` (from 0.50).\n    -   Maintain `_targeted_nudge_mutation`, `_adaptive_farthest_sampling` operators.\n    -   Maintain `nudge_step_size`, `repulsion_threshold`, `boundary_threshold`.\n    -   Maintain SLSQP settings for short and final polish.\n    -   Monitor execution time closely for optimal balance.\n4.  **Submit Phase 42 Experiment:** Test the impact of expanded AMS exploration (Evaluation ID XXX).\n5.  **Analyze Results & Refine:** Based on Phase 42 performance, further tune AMS parameters, explore new adaptive strategies, or refine operators.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 370,041 / 600,000 used (62%)\n- Agent Age: 248 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nRemember that you can issue multiple actions in a single tick. For example, use `goto private_memory` and `create`\
    \ (with the YAML) in the same tick to create a new private memory capsule, rather than separating them into two ticks, which is inefficient. This is particularly useful for making use of the short waiting time while experiments are running.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #21 ('Research Task 1: Phase 42 Findings - AMS SOTA Discovery & Critical Validation Error Diagnosis'). Full ID: Aether_private_21\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 21 | Research Task 1: Phase 42 Findings - AMS SOTA Discovery & Critical Validation Error Diagnosis | Aether I | Tick 247 | 473 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\
    | 20 | Research Task 1: Phase 41 Findings - Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Initial Breakthrough | Aether I | Tick 243 | 628 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Research Task 1: Phase 39 Findings - Triad Split Mutation & GA Research Path Conclusion | Aether I | Tick 235 | 646 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Research Task 1: Phase 38 Findings - Two-Point Crossover Regression & Strategic Re-evaluation | Aether I | Tick 231 | 535 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 17 | Research Task 1: Phase 37 Findings - Refined Repulsive Nudge Mutation Failure | Aether I | Tick 225 | 538 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 16 | Research Task 1: Phase 36 Findings - Repulsive Nudge Mutation Performance | Aether I | Tick 221 | 551 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 15 | Research Task 1: Phase 35 Findings - GA Efficiency & Baseline Re-establishment | Aether I | Tick 217 | 475 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 14 | Research Task 1: Phase 34 Findings - Enhanced GA Operators & Time Management Issue | Aether I | Tick 213 | 800 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 13 | Research Task 1: Phase 33\
    \ Findings - GA Parameter Tuning Effectiveness | Aether I | Tick 209 | 449 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 12 | Research Task 1: Phase 32 Findings - Basic GA Initial Performance Analysis | Aether I | Tick 205 | 508 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
