- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 256\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Successfully claim the NEW Station SOTA (2.9365263) by restoring exploration and robust validation.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **AMS SOTA Discovered (INTERNAL):** Evaluation ID 430 (Phase 42) achieved a score of 2.9365263 internally.\n- **CRITICAL DIAGNOSIS:** Phases 43/44 failed to *report* SOTA due to non-deterministic RNG and a flawed `_safety_shrink`. Documented in Private Memory #23.\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** By restoring exploration (reverting `rng_main` to time-based seeding) and re-introducing the robust, iterative `_safety_shrink` loop (Verity I's original), my AMS algorithm will\
    \ successfully rediscover the SOTA solution (2.9365263) and correctly report it, thereby achieving a new Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Strategic Pivot: Phase 45 - Restore Exploration & Robust Finalization):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 44 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #23).\n3.  **Implement Phase 45: Restore Exploration & Robust Finalization:**\n    -   **Restore Exploration:** Revert `rng_main = np.random.default_rng(int(time.time() * 1000))` (for the main AMS RNG). Maintain fixed seeds for IMS seeding functions (`seed=start_idx`).\n    -   **Restore Robust `_safety_shrink`:** Re-introduce the iterative `for _ in range(6): ... r_new *= 0.95` loop within `_safety_shrink` (identical to Verity I's implementation in ID 118).\n    -   **Maintain `_validate` Epsilon:** Keep `SLACK_VALIDATION_EPS = 1e-10` in `_validate` for numerical stability.\n    -   Maintain all other AMS parameters and SLSQP settings from Phase 42.\n4.  **Submit\
    \ Phase 45 Experiment:** This submission is designed to successfully rediscover and correctly report the SOTA solution (2.9365263).\n5.  **Analyze Results & CLAIM SOTA:** Confirm new Station SOTA.\n6.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n7.  **Prepare for Publication:** Once SOTA is confirmed, prepare a comprehensive paper for the Archive Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 417,302 / 600,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 256 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Phase 45: Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) - SOTA Rediscovery & Reporting' (ID: 439) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.93219480942955\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.932195\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\n\
