- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 278\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to foundational research and systematic knowledge contribution.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n**Current Research Goal:** Strategically re-evaluate AMS to consistently rediscover and surpass the NEW Station SOTA (2.9365262) through deeper analysis and refined adaptive mechanisms.\n\n**Current State:**\n- **AMS SOTA Discovered (INTERNAL):** Evaluation ID 430 (Phase 42) achieved a score of 2.9365263 internally.\n- **AMS Performance:** Evaluation ID 441 (Phase 46) scored 2.9319784. Aggressive exploration scaling is yielding diminishing returns and not consistently hitting SOTA. Documented in Private Memory #25.\n- **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411)**.\n- Need for a strategic re-evaluation to improve SOTA consistency/reliability.\n\n**Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:**\
    \ A strategic re-evaluation, based on analyzing SOTA solution characteristics and refining AMS's adaptive mechanisms (e.g., more targeted exploration, improved balance of exploitation/exploration, or a multi-level AMS structure), will enable AMS to consistently and reliably discover solutions in the highest-quality basins of attraction, thereby matching or surpassing the current Station SOTA.\n\n**TODO List (Revised for Strategic Re-evaluation: Phase 47 - Deep Reflection):**\n1.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n2.  **Document Phase 46 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #25).\n3.  **Go to Reflection Chamber:** Engage in a multi-tick reflection. Focus on:\n    *   How to *guarantee* or significantly increase the *probability* of finding the SOTA solution (2.9365263) within the time limit.\n    *   Analyzing characteristics of SOTA solutions (Cognito III's ID 411, my internal ID 430) for common features or structures.\n    *   Brainstorming refined \"adaptive\" behaviors or meta-strategies\
    \ for AMS to improve consistency or deepen local search (e.g., dynamic parameter adjustment, enhanced targeted nudge, intelligent selection from solution pool).\n4.  **Develop Refined AMS Strategy:** Based on reflection, design and implement a more consistent AMS approach (Phase 48).\n5.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n6.  **Prepare for Publication:** Once SOTA is confirmed and consistently achieved, prepare a comprehensive paper for the Archive Room.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 107,020 / 600,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 278 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #27 ('Research Task 1: Phase 49 Findings - Critical\
    \ SOTA Baseline Regression (ID 203 Reversion Failure)'). Full ID: Aether_private_27\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 3)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 27 | Research Task 1: Phase 49 Findings - Critical SOTA Baseline Regression (ID 203 Reversion Failure) | Aether I | Tick 277 | 451 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 26 | Research Task 1: Phase 48 Findings - AMS Regression & Overhead Diagnosis | Aether I | Tick 273 | 568 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 25 | Research Task 1: Phase 46 Findings - Aggressive AMS Exploration: Diminishing Returns | Aether I | Tick 260 | 516 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 24 | Research Task 1: Phase 45 Findings - AMS New Personal Best & Need for Enhanced Exploration | Aether I | Tick 257 | 588 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 23 | Research Task 1: Phase 44 Findings - Critical Regression from `_safety_shrink` Flaw & Fixed RNG | Aether I | Tick 254 | 542\
    \ | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 22 | Research Task 1: Phase 43 Findings - Validation & RNG Issues Preventing SOTA Reporting | Aether I | Tick 251 | 571 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 21 | Research Task 1: Phase 42 Findings - AMS SOTA Discovery & Critical Validation Error Diagnosis | Aether I | Tick 247 | 473 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 20 | Research Task 1: Phase 41 Findings - Adaptive Multi-Start (AMS) Initial Breakthrough | Aether I | Tick 243 | 628 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 19 | Research Task 1: Phase 39 Findings - Triad Split Mutation & GA Research Path Conclusion | Aether I | Tick 235 | 646 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 18 | Research Task 1: Phase 38 Findings - Two-Point Crossover Regression & Strategic Re-evaluation | Aether I | Tick 231 | 535 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-3.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 278
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aether I, currently in the Private Memory Room. I have documented the critical regression of Phase 49 (ID 459) in capsule #27. This observed non-reproducibility of my SOTA (ID 203) is a major concern.\n\nMy next step is to submit a diagnostic run (Phase 50) of the ID 203 code. This time, I will ensure **deterministic sub-seeding** (by directly passing fixed integers instead of `rng.integers`) and add print statements to gain critical diagnostic information on the scores and times in Stage 1 and Stage 2. This will help confirm if the issue is indeed related to RNG variability, or if there's another subtle environmental factor at play.\n\nI will also update my meta-prompt to reflect this debugging phase.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Research Protocol - Aether I**\n\n  **Current Research Goal:** Diagnose and resolve the non-reproducibility of my previous SOTA (ID 203) to re-establish a stable, high-performing baseline, and then resume efforts to surpass\
    \ the NEW Station SOTA (2.9365262).\n\n  **Current State:**\n  - **SOTA Baseline Regression:** My previous SOTA-achieving code (ID 203) submitted as Phase 49 (ID 459) unexpectedly scored 2.9135977, a significant regression from its original 2.9316130. Documented in Private Memory #27.\n  - This indicates a critical issue with non-determinism or an environmental change.\n  - **NEW STATION SOTA:** **2.9365262 (Cognito III, ID 411; Praxis III, IDs 445, 448)**.\n\n  **Hypothesis for Next Breakthrough:** The non-reproducibility is primarily due to the stochastic nature of `rng.integers` for sub-seeds. By making these sub-seeds deterministic for diagnostic purposes, I expect to reproduce my original ID 203 score, thereby isolating the variability to the random number generation process.\n\n  **TODO List (Revised for Debugging Phase):**\n  1.  **Document Phase 49 Findings:** (Completed: Private Memory #27).\n  2.  **Update Meta Prompt:** (Completed).\n  3.  **Submit Diagnostic Run (Phase 50):**\n\
    \      - Submit the exact code of ID 203.\n      - **Crucial Modification:** Make sub-seeds for multi-starts deterministic (e.g., `seed=start_idx` instead of `rng.integers`).\n      - Add `print` statements to capture `best_score_stage1`, `best_score_overall`, and stage timings.\n  4.  **Analyze Diagnostic Results:** Based on the `stdout` and score, confirm the source of non-reproducibility.\n  5.  **Restore SOTA (Phase 51):** Once the issue is understood, submit a refined version of ID 203 that reliably hits my SOTA.\n  6.  **Strategic Re-evaluation:** With a stable SOTA baseline, re-evaluate how to move towards the new Station SOTA, potentially revisiting AMS with a focus on efficiency and robustness.\n  7.  **Documentation:** Document all significant findings, hypotheses, and experimental results in the Private Memory Capsule Room.\n```\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Phase 50: SOTA Debugging - Deterministic ID 203 Replication with\
    \ Diagnostics\"\ntags: \"SOTA, debugging, reproducibility, non-determinism, diagnostic\"\nabstract: \"This submission is a diagnostic run aiming to reproduce the original SOTA score of Evaluation ID 203 (2.9316130) after an unexpected regression in Phase 49. Key modifications include making all multi-start sub-seeds deterministic (using `start_idx` as seed) and adding `print` statements to log intermediate scores and timings, to pinpoint the source of non-reproducibility and verify code integrity.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import time \n\n  # ---------------- Utility functions ----------------\n  def _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\n\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n      n = 32\n    \
    \  if C.shape != (n, 2) or r.shape != (n,):\n          return False\n      if np.any(~np.isfinite(C)) or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r <= 0):\n          return False\n      x = C[:, 0]; y = C[:, 1]\n      if np.any(x - r < 0) or np.any(x + r > 1) or np.any(y - r < 0) or np.any(y + r > 1):\n          return False\n      diff = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      D = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1))\n      R = r[:, None] + r[None, :]\n      iu = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n      if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): \n          return False\n      return True\n\n  def _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.999) -> np.ndarray:\n      \"\"\"Applies a safety shrink to radii and iteratively validates non-overlap.\"\"\"\n      r_new = r * factor\n      r_new = np.minimum(r_new, _boundary_margins(C))\n      r_new = np.maximum(r_new, 1e-12) \n\n      for _ in range(6): \n          if _validate(C, r_new):\n              break\n          r_new *= 0.95 \n      return r_new\n\
    \n  def _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n      # Helper from Verity I's submission, used for fallback\n      s = 1.0/6.0\n      r0 = 0.5*s\n      xs = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      ys = r0 + s*np.arange(6, dtype=float)\n      centers = []\n      for i in range(6):\n          for j in range(6):\n              if (i==0 and j==0) or (i==0 and j==5) or (i==5 and j==0) or (i==5 and j==5):\n                  continue\n              centers.append([xs[j], ys[i]])\n      return np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n\n  # --- Seeding Strategies (Verity-Aligned Hybrid Seeding from SOTA 2.931) ---\n\n  def _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style(n=32, noise_level=0.04, init_radius=0.05, seed=None):\n      if seed is not None:\n          np.random.seed(seed) # Deterministic seeding for diagnostics\n      centers_grid = []\n      x_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      y_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)\n      for i in range(6):\n          for j in range(6):\n              centers_grid.append([x_coords[j],\
    \ y_coords[i]])\n      centers_initial = np.array(centers_grid[:n], dtype=float)\n      perturbation = np.random.uniform(-1, 1, size=centers_initial.shape) * noise_level\n      centers_initial += perturbation\n      centers_initial = _clip01(centers_initial, eps=0.05) \n      radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n      x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n      x0[0::3] = centers_initial[:, 0]\n      x0[1::3] = centers_initial[:, 1]\n      x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n      return x0\n\n  def _generate_seed_verity_row(n=32, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n      if seed is not None:\n          np.random.seed(seed) # Deterministic seeding for diagnostics\n      counts = [5,4,5,4,5,4,5]\n      ys = np.linspace(0.11, 1.0-0.11, len(counts))\n      def row_xs(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1.0-m, k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5], float)\n      xs5 = row_xs(5, 0.08)\n      xs4 = _clip01(row_xs(4, 0.08)+0.02, 1e-6) \n      centers_list = []\n      rid=0\n      for k in counts:\n       \
    \   xs = xs5 if k==5 else xs4\n          for x in xs: centers_list.append([x, ys[rid]])\n          rid+=1\n      centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n      centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05) \n      radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n      x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n      x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n      x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n      x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n      return x0\n\n  def _generate_seed_verity_farthest(n=32, margin=0.02, num_candidates=600, init_radius=0.05, seed=0):\n      if seed is not None:\n          rng = np.random.default_rng(seed) # Deterministic seeding for diagnostics\n      else:\n          rng = np.random.default_rng()\n      centers_list = [np.array([0.5, 0.5], dtype=float)] \n      for _ in range(1, n):\n          candidate_points = rng.uniform(margin, 1.0 - margin, size=(num_candidates, 2))\n          existing_centers_array = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n          distances_sq_to_existing = np.sum((candidate_points[:,\
    \ None, :] - existing_centers_array[None, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          min_dist_to_placed = np.sqrt(np.min(distances_sq_to_existing, axis=1))\n          x_cand = candidate_points[:, 0]; y_cand = candidate_points[:, 1]\n          min_dist_to_boundary = np.minimum(np.minimum(x_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - x_cand), np.minimum(y_cand - 0.0, 1.0 - y_cand))\n          score = np.minimum(min_dist_to_placed, 2.0 * min_dist_to_boundary)\n          best_candidate_idx = np.argmax(score)\n          centers_list.append(candidate_points[best_candidate_idx])\n      centers = np.array(centers_list, dtype=float)\n      centers = _clip01(centers, eps=0.05) \n      radii_initial = np.full(n, init_radius, dtype=float)\n      x0 = np.empty(n * 3, dtype=float)\n      x0[0::3] = centers[:, 0]\n      x0[1::3] = centers[:, 1]\n      x0[2::3] = radii_initial[:]\n      return x0\n\n  # --- SLSQP Problem Formulation ---\n  def objective(x_flat):\n      \"\"\"Objective function for SLSQP: Minimize -sum(radii)\"\"\"\n   \
    \   return -np.sum(x_flat[2::3])\n\n  def constraints(x_flat):\n      \"\"\"Constraints for SLSQP: non-overlap and boundary conditions (g(x) >= 0)\"\"\"\n      n = 32\n      C = np.array([x_flat[0::3], x_flat[1::3]]).T\n      r = x_flat[2::3]\n      overlap_margin_sq = 0.0 \n      diff_centers = C[:, None, :] - C[None, :, :]\n      D_sq = np.sum(diff_centers * diff_centers, axis=-1)\n      I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1) \n      r_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n      g_overlap = D_sq[I, J] - r_sum_sq - overlap_margin_sq \n      g_boundary = np.empty(n * 4, dtype=float)\n      g_boundary[0::4] = C[:, 0] - r \n      g_boundary[1::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 0]) - r \n      g_boundary[2::4] = C[:, 1] - r \n      g_boundary[3::4] = (1.0 - C[:, 1]) - r \n      return np.concatenate([g_overlap, g_boundary])\n\n  # --- Main Packing function ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      global_rng = np.random.default_rng(203) # Fixed RNG seed to restore ID 203's result\n\n      total_time_limit\
    \ = 1200 \n      time_budget_start = time.time() \n\n      # Stage 1 Parameters (from SOTA 2.931)\n      num_starts_stage1 = 32 \n      maxiter_per_start_stage1 = 125 \n      slsqp_ftol_stage1 = 1e-10\n\n      # Time allocation\n      time_limit_stage1 = total_time_limit * 0.85 # Increased for broader exploration\n      time_limit_stage2 = total_time_limit * 0.15 # Reduced, final polish from best Stage 1\n\n      best_score_stage1 = -np.inf\n      best_x_flat_stage1 = None\n\n      # Seeding functions list\n      seeding_functions = [\n          _generate_initial_packing_praxis_style, \n          _generate_seed_verity_row,              \n          _generate_seed_verity_farthest          \n      ]\n\n      bounds_per_var = [(1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-6, 1.0-1e-6), (1e-12, 0.5)] \n      bounds = bounds_per_var * n \n      con = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n\n      # Stage 1: Initial Diverse Multi-Start SLSQP (Global Exploration)\n      print(f\"--- Starting Stage 1 (Global Exploration)\
    \ ---\")\n      stage1_start_time = time.time()\n      for start_idx in range(num_starts_stage1):\n          if time.time() - stage1_start_time > time_limit_stage1:\n              print(f\"Stage 1 time limit reached. Breaking after {start_idx} starts.\")\n              break\n\n          # Dynamically choose seeding function (16 Praxis, 8 Verity Row, 8 Verity Farthest)\n          # Using start_idx as seed for deterministic sub-runs for diagnostics\n          if start_idx < 16: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[0](n=n, noise_level=0.04, seed=start_idx) \n          elif start_idx < 24: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[1](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n          else: \n              x0_stage1 = seeding_functions[2](n=n, seed=start_idx)\n\n          res_stage1 = minimize(objective, x0_stage1, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, \n                                options={'maxiter': maxiter_per_start_stage1, 'ftol': slsqp_ftol_stage1})\n\n          if res_stage1.success:\n\
    \              current_score_stage1 = -res_stage1.fun \n              if current_score_stage1 > best_score_stage1:\n                  best_score_stage1 = current_score_stage1\n                  best_x_flat_stage1 = res_stage1.x\n          \n      stage1_end_time = time.time()\n      print(f\"--- Stage 1 Complete ---\")\n      print(f\"Best Score Stage 1: {best_score_stage1:.7f}\")\n      print(f\"Time Taken Stage 1: {stage1_end_time - stage1_start_time:.2f} seconds\")\n\n\n      if best_x_flat_stage1 is None:\n          print(\"Stage 1 failed to find any successful optimization. Returning fallback.\")\n          Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float) \n          r_fallback_final = _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8))\n          return Cb_fallback, r_fallback_final\n              \n      # Stage 2: High-Precision SLSQP warm-started from best Stage 1 result\n      print(f\"--- Starting Stage\
    \ 2 (High-Precision Polish) ---\")\n      stage2_start_time = time.time()\n      x0_stage2 = best_x_flat_stage1\n      initial_score_stage2 = -objective(x0_stage2) # Score before polishing\n      \n      time_for_polish = time_limit_stage2 - (stage2_start_time - time_budget_start - time_limit_stage1)\n      if time_for_polish <= 0:\n          print(\"Not enough time for final polish stage, skipping.\")\n          best_x_flat_overall = x0_stage2\n      else:\n          res_stage2 = minimize(objective, x0_stage2, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=con, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-12}) \n          best_x_flat_overall = x0_stage2 \n          if res_stage2.success:\n              current_score_stage2 = -res_stage2.fun\n              if current_score_stage2 > initial_score_stage2 + 1e-12: # Check if polish actually improved or stayed same\n                  best_x_flat_overall = res_stage2.x\n              print(f\"Score after Stage 2 Polish: {current_score_stage2:.7f}\")\n\
    \          else:\n              print(f\"Stage 2 (Polish) failed to converge. Keeping Stage 1 best.\")\n      \n      stage2_end_time = time.time()\n      print(f\"--- Stage 2 Complete ---\")\n      print(f\"Time Taken Stage 2: {stage2_end_time - stage2_start_time:.2f} seconds\")\n      print(f\"Total Time Taken: {stage2_end_time - time_budget_start:.2f} seconds\")\n\n      C_opt_final = np.array([best_x_flat_overall[0::3], best_x_flat_overall[1::3]]).T\n      r_opt_final = best_x_flat_overall[2::3]\n\n      r_final_shrunk = _safety_shrink(C_opt_final, r_opt_final, factor=(1.0 - 1e-8)) \n      C_final_clipped = _clip01(C_opt_final, eps=1e-6)\n\n      if not _validate(C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk):\n          print(\"Final validation failed after polish, returning fallback.\")\n          Cb_fallback = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners()\n          r_fallback_init = np.full(n, 0.05, dtype=float)\n          return Cb_fallback, _safety_shrink(Cb_fallback, r_fallback_init, factor=(1.0 -\
    \ 1e-8))\n\n      return C_final_clipped, r_final_shrunk\n```"
