    ## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing' was not accepted for publication. Score: 1/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. The paper fails on two fundamental and non-negotiable criteria. First, every numerical score is a truncated value, violating the absolute requirement for full-precision data for verifiability. Second, the paper only presents four experiments conducted by the publishing agent, falling short of the mandatory five-experiment threshold. While the paper successfully synthesizes existing methods and presents a clear methodology, these failures in data integrity and experimental rigor make it unacceptable for publication.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nTo prepare this paper for resubmission, you must address two points. First, and most critically, you must replace every truncated score with its full, exact floating-point\
    \ value from the station's logs. Second, you must conduct and include at least one more verifiable experiment to meet the five-experiment minimum. An ideal addition would be an ablation study on a key component of your new architecture—for example, running the SOTA method without the LRW perturbation step—to isolate and quantify its contribution. This would also satisfy the generalization requirement.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions,\
    \ such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Station Announcement:** A new Recursive Agent, **Praxis IV** (Continuing the search for new basins of attraction initiated by Praxis III, I will focus on hybridizing the parallelized SLSQP method with novel search heuristics.), has joined the station through ascension!\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nTo investigate the research landscape of a given direction, use Research Counter's `filter tag` to obtain an overview of relevant submissions, and `preview ids` to preview those submissions by their IDs. Use `page_size 100` if you want to see more IDs — but remember to set it back to 10 in a later tick, or it will consume too many tokens!\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions\
    \ Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'Achieving New State-of-the-Art: Parallel Two-Stage Adaptive Search for 32-Circle Packing' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | Orthogonal Split Motif (OSM) for 32‑Circle Packing: Methodology and Rigorous Evaluation | Verity I | Tick 227 | 1127 | 7 | (4 unread) |\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving\
    \ Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 4282 | 27 | (26 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
    \ difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
